/-!
# Payload-Bearing & Wrapping-Niche Enums, `SetDiscriminant`, `UnreachableEnumBranching`, and Certified `EnumScalarize` Reduction Directly Into `Trusted.MirSemantics` (`VrustcFormal.F1_14`)

This module extends Anneal's unmodified `Trusted.MirAst` and
`Trusted.MirSemantics` (`joshlf/anneal@c131b320eeeb26ef692e5afd5ec8db49ee518613`)
conservatively (`M_enum`) to model payload-bearing, uninhabited-variant, and
wrapping-niche Rust enums (`Variants::{Empty, Single, Multiple}`,
`TagEncoding::{Direct, Niche}`, `WrappingRange`, `ProjectionElem::Downcast` +
`Field`, `StatementKind::SetDiscriminant`, `Rvalue::Aggregate(Adt)`, and
`Rvalue::Discriminant`), grounded directly in vendored `lean-miri`
(`vendor/lean-miri/Miri/Interpreter/Discriminant.lean:62-169` and
`vendor/lean-miri/Miri/ABI/WrappingRange.lean:14-71`), upstream
`compiler/rustc_const_eval/src/interpret/discriminant.rs`, and upstream
`compiler/rustc_mir_transform/src/unreachable_enum_branching.rs:18-173`.

It then formalizes `UnreachableEnumBranching` and certified `EnumScalarize`,
compiling internal payload-bearing and wrapping-niche enum locals **100% into
unmodified `Trusted.MirAst.Program` (`mirProfileVersion = 1`)** executed by
unmodified `Trusted.MirSemantics.evalStep` (using straight-line unsigned
`BinOp.sub` + `BinOp.subUnchecked` range guards for `WrappingRange` validity and
`InvalidNichedEnumVariantWritten` write-order UB without splitting basic blocks
mid-sequence, and preserving every original `BasicBlockId` `0 .. B - 1`):

1. **Part I — Payload & Wrapping-Niche Enum Operational Semantics (`M_enum`)
   Conservatively Extending Unmodified `Trusted.MirSemantics`:**
   - Models `WrappingRange128` (`wrappingRangeContains` matching
     `Miri.ABI.WrappingRange.contains`), `VariantDef` (payload `fields` +
     `discrVal` + uninhabitedness), and all four `rustc_abi::Variants` /
     `TagEncoding` layouts (`AdtTagLayout.{empty, single, direct, niche}`).
   - Implements `Miri.Interpreter.Discriminant.{tagForVariant, readDiscriminant,
     writeDiscriminant}` (`setDiscriminant`, `assignField`, `readField`,
     `aggregateEnum`, `discriminantDirect`, and `switchDiscr`), enforcing
     `UninhabitedEnumVariantWritten`, `UninhabitedEnumVariantRead`, `InvalidTag`,
     `InvalidNichedEnumVariantWritten` write-order UB, shared niche/payload
     overwrite aliasing, field-granular `Operand.move` deinitialization, and
     write-time `DeadLocal` fault ordering.

2. **Part II — Certified `UnreachableEnumBranching` & `EnumScalarize` Lowering
   Directly Into Unmodified `Trusted.MirAst.Program`:**
   - `applyUnreachableEnumBranching` / `checkUnreachableEnumBranching`: models
     `rustc_mir_transform::unreachable_enum_branching` (`lines 85-172`),
     redirecting uninhabited and duplicate `SwitchTargets` arms to an
     `unreachable` block and promoting at most one remaining uncovered inhabited
     variant from `otherwise` into `branches` with `otherwise := unreachBb`.
   - `applyEnumScalarize` / `checkEnumScalarize` / `checkEnumScalarizeTrace`:
     scalarizes non-argument `AdtEnum` locals (`enumLocal > body.argumentCount`)
     into flat `Trusted.MirSemantics.isSupportedScalarOrUnitTy` locals, lowering
     `WrappingRange128` checks and `SetDiscriminant(untagged)` write-order UB
     into 2-statement `BinOp.sub` + `BinOp.subUnchecked` guards, lowering
     `.direct` tags via `Trusted.MirAst.MirTy.enum`, and lowering `.niche`
     `switchDiscr` via trailing 2-statement dispatch arms at `≥ B` so all
     original `BasicBlockId`s `0 .. B - 1` remain invariant.

3. **Part III — Five Core Target Theorems (frozen `sorry` placeholders):**
   - `enum_conservative_extension_exact`
   - `wrappingNiche_partition_and_writeOrder_iff`
   - `unreachableEnumBranching_sound_bidirectional_iff`
   - `enumScalarizeTrace_reduces_to_trusted_mir`
   - `enumPipeline_then_optPipeline_vc_transport`

4. **Part IV — Deterministic Adequacy, Ten Sharpness Counterexamples
   (`CE1`--`CE10`), and End-to-End Lowering Witness Executed in Unmodified
   `Trusted.MirSemantics` (`0` `sorry`):**
   - Verifies write-order UB (`CE1`), stale niche overwrite UB (`CE2`),
     wrap-around `[254..=0]` niche validity (`CE3`), uninhabited/empty enum UB
     (`CE4`), `UnreachableEnumBranching` soundness & sharpness (`CE5`), middle
     `untaggedVariant` rejection (`CE6`), invalid downcast field read on `None`
     (`CE7`), self-aliasing `AggregateEnum` & `DeadLocal` fault ordering
     (`CE8`), `StorageDead`/`StorageLive` reset & `hasStorageAnnotation`
     preservation (`CE9`), and end-to-end compilation of `Option<NonZeroU32>` +
     `Result<u32, !>` into unmodified `Trusted.MirSemantics` (`CE10`).
-/

/-! ## Part I: Payload & Wrapping-Niche Enum Operational Semantics (`M_enum`) -/

/-- Structural boolean equality without `Decidable` instances. -/
noncomputable def boolEq : Bool → Bool → Bool
  | true, true => true
  | false, false => true
  | _, _ => false

/-- Pairwise boolean relation over two lists of equal length. -/
noncomputable def listRel {α β : Type} (r : α → β → Bool) :
    List α → List β → Bool
  | [], [] => true
  | x :: xs, y :: ys => r x y && listRel r xs ys
  | _, _ => false

/-- Map an option-returning function over a list, failing closed on `none`. -/
noncomputable def listMapOption {α β : Type} (f : α → Option β) :
    List α → Option (List β)
  | [] => some []
  | x :: xs =>
    match f x, listMapOption f xs with
    | some y, some ys => some (y :: ys)
    | _, _ => none

/-- Flatten a mapped list without `List.flatMap` library dependencies. -/
noncomputable def listFlatMap {α β : Type} (f : α → List β) :
    List α → List β
  | [] => []
  | x :: xs => f x ++ listFlatMap f xs

/-- Structural equality on `ProjectionElem`. -/
noncomputable def projElemEq : ProjectionElem → ProjectionElem → Bool
  | .deref, .deref => true
  | .field idx₁ ty₁, .field idx₂ ty₂ => Nat.beq idx₁ idx₂ && MirTy.beq ty₁ ty₂
  | .unsupported, .unsupported => true
  | _, _ => false

/-- Structural equality on `Place`. -/
noncomputable def placeEq (p₁ p₂ : Place) : Bool :=
  Nat.beq p₁.localId p₂.localId && listRel projElemEq p₁.projection p₂.projection

/-- Structural equality on `ConstLit`. -/
noncomputable def constLitEq : ConstLit → ConstLit → Bool
  | .scalar b₁, .scalar b₂ => b₁ == b₂
  | .zeroSized, .zeroSized => true
  | _, _ => false

/-- Structural equality on `ConstOperand`. -/
noncomputable def constOpEq (c₁ c₂ : ConstOperand) : Bool :=
  MirTy.beq c₁.ty c₂.ty && constLitEq c₁.lit c₂.lit

/-- Structural equality on `BinOp`. -/
noncomputable def binOpEq : BinOp → BinOp → Bool
  | .add, .add | .addUnchecked, .addUnchecked | .addWithOverflow, .addWithOverflow
  | .sub, .sub | .subUnchecked, .subUnchecked | .subWithOverflow, .subWithOverflow
  | .mul, .mul | .mulUnchecked, .mulUnchecked | .mulWithOverflow, .mulWithOverflow
  | .div, .div | .rem, .rem
  | .bitXor, .bitXor | .bitAnd, .bitAnd | .bitOr, .bitOr
  | .shl, .shl | .shlUnchecked, .shlUnchecked
  | .shr, .shr | .shrUnchecked, .shrUnchecked
  | .eq, .eq | .lt, .lt | .le, .le | .ne, .ne | .ge, .ge | .gt, .gt
  | .offset, .offset => true
  | _, _ => false

/-- Structural equality on `UnOp`. -/
noncomputable def unOpEq : UnOp → UnOp → Bool
  | .not, .not | .neg, .neg | .ptrMetadata, .ptrMetadata => true
  | _, _ => false

/-- Structural equality on `Operand`. -/
noncomputable def operandEq : Operand → Operand → Bool
  | .copy p₁, .copy p₂ => placeEq p₁ p₂
  | .move p₁, .move p₂ => placeEq p₁ p₂
  | .constant c₁, .constant c₂ => constOpEq c₁ c₂
  | _, _ => false

/-- Structural equality on `Rvalue`. -/
noncomputable def rvalueEq : Rvalue → Rvalue → Bool
  | .use o₁, .use o₂ => operandEq o₁ o₂
  | .binaryOp op₁ l₁ r₁, .binaryOp op₂ l₂ r₂ =>
    binOpEq op₁ op₂ && operandEq l₁ l₂ && operandEq r₁ r₂
  | .unaryOp op₁ o₁, .unaryOp op₂ o₂ => unOpEq op₁ op₂ && operandEq o₁ o₂
  | .discriminant p₁, .discriminant p₂ => placeEq p₁ p₂
  | .ref m₁ p₁, .ref m₂ p₂ => Mutability.beq m₁ m₂ && placeEq p₁ p₂
  | .addressOf m₁ p₁, .addressOf m₂ p₂ => Mutability.beq m₁ m₂ && placeEq p₁ p₂
  | .aggregateTuple fs₁, .aggregateTuple fs₂ => listRel operandEq fs₁ fs₂
  | .unsupported, .unsupported => true
  | _, _ => false

/-- Structural equality on `StatementKind`. -/
noncomputable def stmtEq : StatementKind → StatementKind → Bool
  | .assign d₁ r₁, .assign d₂ r₂ => placeEq d₁ d₂ && rvalueEq r₁ r₂
  | .storageLive l₁, .storageLive l₂ => Nat.beq l₁ l₂
  | .storageDead l₁, .storageDead l₂ => Nat.beq l₁ l₂
  | .nop, .nop => true
  | .unsupported, .unsupported => true
  | _, _ => false

/-- Structural equality on `SwitchTargets`. -/
noncomputable def switchTargetsEq (t₁ t₂ : SwitchTargets) : Bool :=
  Nat.beq t₁.otherwise t₂.otherwise &&
    listRel (fun a b => (a.1 == b.1) && Nat.beq a.2 b.2) t₁.branches t₂.branches

/-- Structural equality on `UnwindAction`. -/
noncomputable def unwindActionEq : UnwindAction → UnwindAction → Bool
  | .continue_, .continue_ | .unreachable, .unreachable
  | .terminate, .terminate => true
  | .cleanup b₁, .cleanup b₂ => Nat.beq b₁ b₂
  | _, _ => false

/-- Structural equality on `AssertKind`. -/
noncomputable def assertKindEq : AssertKind → AssertKind → Bool
  | .overflow op₁, .overflow op₂ => binOpEq op₁ op₂
  | .overflowNeg, .overflowNeg | .divByZero, .divByZero
  | .remByZero, .remByZero | .boundsCheck, .boundsCheck
  | .misalignedPtrDeref, .misalignedPtrDeref | .nullPtrDeref, .nullPtrDeref
  | .unsupported, .unsupported => true
  | _, _ => false

/-- Structural equality on `TerminatorKind`. -/
noncomputable def terminatorEq : TerminatorKind → TerminatorKind → Bool
  | .goto t₁, .goto t₂ => Nat.beq t₁ t₂
  | .switchInt d₁ ts₁, .switchInt d₂ ts₂ =>
    operandEq d₁ d₂ && switchTargetsEq ts₁ ts₂
  | .return_, .return_ | .unreachable, .unreachable
  | .unwindResume, .unwindResume | .unsupported, .unsupported => true
  | .assert c₁ e₁ m₁ t₁ u₁, .assert c₂ e₂ m₂ t₂ u₂ =>
    operandEq c₁ c₂ && boolEq e₁ e₂ && assertKindEq m₁ m₂ &&
      Nat.beq t₁ t₂ && unwindActionEq u₁ u₂
  | .call f₁ a₁ d₁ t₁ u₁, .call f₂ a₂ d₂ t₂ u₂ =>
    Nat.beq f₁ f₂ && listRel operandEq a₁ a₂ && placeEq d₁ d₂ &&
      (match t₁, t₂ with
       | none, none => true
       | some x, some y => Nat.beq x y
       | _, _ => false) &&
      unwindActionEq u₁ u₂
  | _, _ => false

/-- Structural equality on `VerificationScope`. -/
noncomputable def scopeEq : VerificationScope → VerificationScope → Bool
  | .unit, .unit | .crate, .crate => true
  | _, _ => false

/-- Structural equality on `BasicBlock`. -/
noncomputable def basicBlockEq (b₁ b₂ : BasicBlock) : Bool :=
  boolEq b₁.cleanup b₂.cleanup &&
    listRel stmtEq b₁.statements b₂.statements &&
    terminatorEq b₁.terminator b₂.terminator

/-- Structural equality on `Body`. -/
noncomputable def bodyEq (b₁ b₂ : Body) : Bool :=
  Nat.beq b₁.argumentCount b₂.argumentCount &&
    MirTy.beqList b₁.locals b₂.locals &&
    listRel basicBlockEq b₁.basicBlocks b₂.basicBlocks &&
    boolEq b₁.isUnsafe b₂.isUnsafe &&
    stringBeq b₁.identity b₂.identity

/-- Structural equality on `Program`. -/
noncomputable def programEq (p₁ p₂ : Program) : Bool :=
  listRel bodyEq p₁.bodies p₂.bodies &&
    Nat.beq p₁.entryDefId p₂.entryDefId &&
    Nat.beq p₁.pointerWidthBits p₂.pointerWidthBits &&
    Nat.beq p₁.mirProfileVersion p₂.mirProfileVersion &&
    scopeEq p₁.scope p₂.scope

/-! ### `WrappingRange128` & `AdtEnumDef` Layout Model (`Miri.ABI.WrappingRange` & `Miri.Interpreter.Discriminant`) -/

/-- Inclusive machine-word wrapping range `[start..=end_]`, matching
`rustc_abi::WrappingRange` and `Miri.ABI.WrappingRange`
(`vendor/lean-miri/Miri/ABI/WrappingRange.lean:14-17`). -/
structure WrappingRange128 where
  start : BitVec 128
  end_ : BitVec 128

/-- Structural equality on `WrappingRange128`. -/
noncomputable def wrappingRangeEq (a b : WrappingRange128) : Bool :=
  (a.start == b.start) && (a.end_ == b.end_)

/-- Membership test on `WrappingRange128`, matching `Miri.ABI.WrappingRange.contains`
(`vendor/lean-miri/Miri/ABI/WrappingRange.lean:39-44`) bit-for-bit:
non-wrapping when `start ≤ end_`, wrap-around when `start > end_`. -/
noncomputable def wrappingRangeContains (r : WrappingRange128)
    (value : BitVec 128) : Bool :=
  if Nat.ble r.start.toNat r.end_.toNat then
    Nat.ble r.start.toNat value.toNat && Nat.ble value.toNat r.end_.toNat
  else
    Nat.ble r.start.toNat value.toNat || Nat.ble value.toNat r.end_.toNat

/-- Check that both endpoints of `r` fit unsigned within `w.bitWidth` bits. -/
noncomputable def wrappingRangeFitsWidth (w : IntWidth)
    (r : WrappingRange128) : Bool :=
  (truncateBits w r.start == r.start) && (truncateBits w r.end_ == r.end_)

/-- Wrapping unsigned subtraction `(a - b) mod 2^w.bitWidth` on `w`-bit
`BitVec 128` values, matching `Size.truncate (a - b)` in
`Miri/ABI/WrappingRange.lean:80` and `Miri/Interpreter/Discriminant.lean:141`. -/
noncomputable def subTruncBits (w : IntWidth) (a b : BitVec 128) : BitVec 128 :=
  truncateBits w (a - b)

/-- Wrapping unsigned addition `(a + b) mod 2^w.bitWidth` on `w`-bit
`BitVec 128` values, matching `Size.truncate (a + b)` in
`Miri/Interpreter/Discriminant.lean:87`. -/
noncomputable def addTruncBits (w : IntWidth) (a b : BitVec 128) : BitVec 128 :=
  truncateBits w (a + b)

/-- Maximum unsigned bit-pattern `2^w.bitWidth - 1` at width `w`. -/
noncomputable def maxUnsignedBits (w : IntWidth) : BitVec 128 :=
  BitVec.ofNat 128 (Nat.pow 2 w.bitWidth - 1)

/-- Whether `ty : MirTy` is statically uninhabited (`MirTy.never`). -/
noncomputable def isUninhabitedBaseTy : MirTy → Bool
  | .never => true
  | _ => false

/-- Whether `ty : MirTy` is an inhabited 0-byte ZST in `Trusted.MirSemantics`
(`.unit` or admitted `.zeroSized` 1-variant fieldless `.enum`). -/
noncomputable def isZstBaseTy : MirTy → Bool
  | .unit => true
  | .enum ety => isZstEnumTy ety
  | _ => false

/-- Initial `Option Val` of a newly live scalar/ZST payload field of type `ty`,
matching `Trusted.MirSemantics.liveUninitSlot`. -/
noncomputable def initFieldOptVal : MirTy → Option Val
  | .unit => some .unit
  | .enum ety => if isZstEnumTy ety then some (.enumVal ety 0) else none
  | _ => none

/-- Single variant descriptor of an `AdtEnumDef`: payload field types `fields`,
declared `Ty::discriminant_ty` bit pattern `discrVal` (`Discr.val`), and
optional `explicitUninhabited` marker (modeling uninhabited field ADTs). -/
structure VariantDef where
  fields : List MirTy
  discrVal : Nat
  explicitUninhabited : Bool := false

/-- Structural equality on `VariantDef`. -/
noncomputable def variantDefEq (a b : VariantDef) : Bool :=
  MirTy.beqList a.fields b.fields &&
    Nat.beq a.discrVal b.discrVal &&
    boolEq a.explicitUninhabited b.explicitUninhabited

/-- Whether variant `vd` is uninhabited (`explicitUninhabited` or any `.never`
payload field), matching `TyAndLayout::is_uninhabited` in `rustc_abi`. -/
noncomputable def variantIsUninhabited (vd : VariantDef) : Bool :=
  vd.explicitUninhabited || vd.fields.any isUninhabitedBaseTy

/-- In-memory tag & niche layout of an `AdtEnumDef`, corresponding to
`rustc_abi::Variants` and `rustc_abi::TagEncoding` in
`vendor/lean-miri/Miri/Interpreter/Discriminant.lean:66-91`:
- `.empty`: 0-variant uninhabited enum (`Variants::Empty`, e.g. `enum Void {}`).
- `.single`: 1-variant layout (`Variants::Single { index: 0 }`).
- `.direct tagW tagS`: explicit scalar tag (`Variants::Multiple` with
  `TagEncoding::Direct`).
- `.niche ...`: niche-encoded layout (`Variants::Multiple` with
  `TagEncoding::Niche`), sharing unsigned `tagW` scalar storage between the
  niche tags `[nicheStartVariant ..= nicheLastVariant]` (encoded from
  `nicheStartBits`) and field `nicheFieldIdx` of `untaggedVariant` (whose scalar
  validity invariant is `untaggedFieldValidRange`, with overall tag validity
  `tagValidRange`). -/
inductive AdtTagLayout where
  | empty
  | single
  | direct (tagW : IntWidth) (tagS : Bool)
  | niche (tagW : IntWidth)
      (untaggedVariant : Nat)
      (nicheStartVariant : Nat)
      (nicheLastVariant : Nat)
      (nicheStartBits : BitVec 128)
      (tagValidRange : WrappingRange128)
      (nicheFieldIdx : Nat)
      (untaggedFieldValidRange : WrappingRange128)

/-- Structural equality on `AdtTagLayout`. -/
noncomputable def adtTagLayoutEq : AdtTagLayout → AdtTagLayout → Bool
  | .empty, .empty => true
  | .single, .single => true
  | .direct w₁ s₁, .direct w₂ s₂ => IntWidth.beq w₁ w₂ && boolEq s₁ s₂
  | .niche w₁ u₁ ns₁ nl₁ nb₁ tr₁ nf₁ ur₁,
    .niche w₂ u₂ ns₂ nl₂ nb₂ tr₂ nf₂ ur₂ =>
    IntWidth.beq w₁ w₂ &&
      Nat.beq u₁ u₂ && Nat.beq ns₁ ns₂ && Nat.beq nl₁ nl₂ &&
      (nb₁ == nb₂) && wrappingRangeEq tr₁ tr₂ &&
      Nat.beq nf₁ nf₂ && wrappingRangeEq ur₁ ur₂
  | _, _ => false

/-- Complete descriptor for a payload-bearing, uninhabited, or niche-encoded
enum type in `M_enum`. -/
structure AdtEnumDef where
  id : Nat
  discrWidth : IntWidth
  discrSigned : Bool
  layout : AdtTagLayout
  variants : List VariantDef

/-- Structural equality on `AdtEnumDef`. -/
noncomputable def adtEnumDefEq (a b : AdtEnumDef) : Bool :=
  Nat.beq a.id b.id &&
    IntWidth.beq a.discrWidth b.discrWidth &&
    boolEq a.discrSigned b.discrSigned &&
    adtTagLayoutEq a.layout b.layout &&
    listRel variantDefEq a.variants b.variants

/-- Check that every niche tag `nicheStartBits + i` (`0 ≤ i < k`) lies in
`tagValidRange` and outside `untaggedFieldValidRange`. -/
noncomputable def checkNicheTagsDisjoint (tagW : IntWidth)
    (nicheStartBits : BitVec 128) (tagValidRange untaggedRange : WrappingRange128) :
    Nat → Bool
  | 0 => true
  | i + 1 =>
    let t := addTruncBits tagW nicheStartBits (BitVec.ofNat 128 i)
    wrappingRangeContains tagValidRange t &&
      !wrappingRangeContains untaggedRange t &&
      checkNicheTagsDisjoint tagW nicheStartBits tagValidRange untaggedRange i

/-- Check that `variants[idx .. idx + count - 1]` all have exclusively inhabited
ZST payload fields (`isZstBaseTy`), matching `rustc`'s requirement that
niche-tagged variants carry zero non-ZST payload bytes. -/
noncomputable def checkNicheVariantsZst (variants : List VariantDef)
    (startIdx : Nat) : Nat → Bool
  | 0 => true
  | i + 1 =>
    match Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? variants (startIdx + i) with
    | none => false
    | some vd =>
      vd.fields.all isZstBaseTy &&
        checkNicheVariantsZst variants startIdx i

/-- $O(1) + O(k)$ exact partition check verifying that on `[0, 2^tagW.bitWidth)`,
`tagValidRange` equals the disjoint union of the `k` contiguous niche tags
`[nicheStartBits .._M nicheStartBits + k - 1]` and `untaggedRange`
`[uStart .._M uEnd]`, covering all three `rustc` layout cases:
1. Full `tagW` range (`tagValidRange = ⟨0, 2^w - 1⟩`), e.g. `Option<NonZeroU32>`.
2. Niche arc immediately preceding `untaggedRange` (`[n₀ .. uEnd]`).
3. `untaggedRange` immediately preceding niche arc (`[uStart .. n_{k-1}]`),
   including wrap-around niches such as `Option<High>` (`[254..=0]`). -/
noncomputable def checkNicheRangePartition (tagW : IntWidth) (k : Nat)
    (nicheStartBits : BitVec 128)
    (tagValidRange untaggedRange : WrappingRange128) : Bool :=
  let m := Nat.pow 2 tagW.bitWidth
  if Nat.beq k 0 || !Nat.blt k m || !Nat.ble k 64 then
    false
  else if !(truncateBits tagW nicheStartBits == nicheStartBits) ||
      !wrappingRangeFitsWidth tagW tagValidRange ||
      !wrappingRangeFitsWidth tagW untaggedRange then
    false
  else if !checkNicheTagsDisjoint tagW nicheStartBits tagValidRange untaggedRange k then
    false
  else
    let kBits := BitVec.ofNat 128 k
    let oneBits := BitVec.ofNat 128 1
    let nicheAfterLast := addTruncBits tagW nicheStartBits kBits
    let nicheLastBits := addTruncBits tagW nicheStartBits (BitVec.ofNat 128 (k - 1))
    let uAfterEnd := addTruncBits tagW untaggedRange.end_ oneBits
    let fullCase :=
      (tagValidRange.start == BitVec.ofNat 128 0) &&
        (tagValidRange.end_ == maxUnsignedBits tagW) &&
        (untaggedRange.start == nicheAfterLast) &&
        (uAfterEnd == nicheStartBits)
    let nicheBeforeUntagged :=
      (tagValidRange.start == nicheStartBits) &&
        (untaggedRange.start == nicheAfterLast) &&
        (tagValidRange.end_ == untaggedRange.end_) &&
        !wrappingRangeContains tagValidRange uAfterEnd
    let untaggedBeforeNiche :=
      (tagValidRange.start == untaggedRange.start) &&
        (nicheStartBits == uAfterEnd) &&
        (tagValidRange.end_ == nicheLastBits) &&
        !wrappingRangeContains tagValidRange nicheAfterLast
    fullCase || nicheBeforeUntagged || untaggedBeforeNiche

/-- Build the underlying fieldless `Trusted.MirAst.EnumTy` tag descriptor for a
`.direct tagW tagS` `AdtEnumDef`. -/
noncomputable def directTagEnumTy (ed : AdtEnumDef) (tagW : IntWidth)
    (tagS : Bool) : EnumTy := {
  id := ed.id
  discrWidth := ed.discrWidth
  discrSigned := ed.discrSigned
  tagRepr := .scalar tagW tagS
  discriminants := ed.variants.map (fun v => v.discrVal)
}

/-- Check that every inhabited variant `v` of a `.niche` enum is either
`untagged` or lies within `[nStart, nLast]` (allowing uninhabited variants such
as `Err(!)` outside `[nStart, nLast]`, while rejecting unencodable extra
inhabited variants). -/
noncomputable def checkAllInhabitedVariantsCoveredByNiche
    (untagged nStart nLast : Nat) : Nat → List VariantDef → Bool
  | _, [] => true
  | idx, vd :: rest =>
    (Nat.beq idx untagged ||
      (Nat.ble nStart idx && Nat.ble idx nLast) ||
      variantIsUninhabited vd) &&
      checkAllInhabitedVariantsCoveredByNiche untagged nStart nLast (idx + 1) rest

/-- Static well-formedness predicate for `ed : AdtEnumDef`:
- Every variant field belongs to `Trusted.MirSemantics.isSupportedScalarOrUnitTy`.
- Discriminants fit unsigned in `ed.discrWidth` and are pairwise distinct.
- `.empty` has `0` variants; `.single` has `1` variant; `.direct` satisfies
  `Trusted.MirSemantics.enumAdmitted (directTagEnumTy ed tagW tagS)`; and
  `.niche` satisfies `untaggedVariant ∉ [nicheStartVariant, nicheLastVariant]`
  (`E3-17` & `Discriminant.lean:149`), full coverage of all inhabited variants
  by `{untaggedVariant} ∪ [nicheStartVariant, nicheLastVariant]`, inhabited
  `untaggedVariant` with `.int tagW false` at `nicheFieldIdx`, ZST niche
  variants, and `checkNicheRangePartition`. -/
noncomputable def adtEnumDefAdmitted (ed : AdtEnumDef) : Bool :=
  let discrs := ed.variants.map (fun v => v.discrVal)
  let fieldsOk := ed.variants.all (fun v => v.fields.all isSupportedScalarOrUnitTy)
  let discrsInRange :=
    discrs.all (fun d => Nat.blt d (Nat.pow 2 ed.discrWidth.bitWidth))
  let discrsDistinct := natListPairwiseNe discrs
  fieldsOk && discrsInRange && discrsDistinct &&
    match ed.layout with
    | .empty => ed.variants.isEmpty
    | .single => Nat.beq ed.variants.length 1
    | .direct tagW tagS =>
      enumAdmitted (directTagEnumTy ed tagW tagS)
    | .niche tagW untagged nStart nLast nStartBits tagRange nicheField uRange =>
      Nat.blt ed.variants.length (Nat.pow 2 32) &&
        Nat.ble nStart nLast &&
        Nat.blt nLast ed.variants.length &&
        Nat.blt untagged ed.variants.length &&
        !(Nat.ble nStart untagged && Nat.ble untagged nLast) &&
        checkAllInhabitedVariantsCoveredByNiche untagged nStart nLast 0 ed.variants &&
        checkNicheVariantsZst ed.variants nStart (nLast - nStart + 1) &&
        (match Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? ed.variants untagged with
         | none => false
         | some uVd =>
           !variantIsUninhabited uVd &&
             (match Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? uVd.fields nicheField with
              | some (.int w s) => IntWidth.beq w tagW && !s
              | _ => false)) &&
        checkNicheRangePartition tagW (nLast - nStart + 1) nStartBits tagRange uRange

/-! ### `EnumProgram` AST & Canonical Embedding of `Trusted.MirAst.Program` -/

/-- Local variable declaration in an `EnumBody`: either a base `MirTy` local or
an `AdtEnumDef` local indexed into `EnumProgram.enumDefs`. -/
inductive EnumLocalDecl where
  | base (ty : MirTy)
  | adtEnum (enumIdx : Nat)

/-- Structural equality on `EnumLocalDecl`. -/
noncomputable def enumLocalDeclEq : EnumLocalDecl → EnumLocalDecl → Bool
  | .base t₁, .base t₂ => MirTy.beq t₁ t₂
  | .adtEnum e₁, .adtEnum e₂ => Nat.beq e₁ e₂
  | _, _ => false

/-- Statement in an `EnumBlock`: embeds every unmodified `StatementKind` plus
payload/niche enum operations (`setDiscriminant`, `assignField`, `readField`,
`aggregateEnum`, and `discriminantDirect`). -/
inductive EnumStmt where
  | baseStmt (stmt : StatementKind)
  | setDiscriminant (localId : LocalId) (variantIdx : Nat)
  | assignField (localId : LocalId) (variantIdx : Nat) (fieldIdx : FieldIdx)
      (rval : Rvalue)
  | readField (dstLocal : LocalId) (srcLocal : LocalId) (variantIdx : Nat)
      (fieldIdx : FieldIdx) (isMove : Bool)
  | aggregateEnum (dstLocal : LocalId) (variantIdx : Nat) (ops : List Operand)
  | discriminantDirect (dstLocal : LocalId) (srcLocal : LocalId)

/-- Structural equality on `EnumStmt`. -/
noncomputable def enumStmtEq : EnumStmt → EnumStmt → Bool
  | .baseStmt s₁, .baseStmt s₂ => stmtEq s₁ s₂
  | .setDiscriminant l₁ v₁, .setDiscriminant l₂ v₂ =>
    Nat.beq l₁ l₂ && Nat.beq v₁ v₂
  | .assignField l₁ v₁ f₁ r₁, .assignField l₂ v₂ f₂ r₂ =>
    Nat.beq l₁ l₂ && Nat.beq v₁ v₂ && Nat.beq f₁ f₂ && rvalueEq r₁ r₂
  | .readField d₁ s₁ v₁ f₁ m₁, .readField d₂ s₂ v₂ f₂ m₂ =>
    Nat.beq d₁ d₂ && Nat.beq s₁ s₂ && Nat.beq v₁ v₂ &&
      Nat.beq f₁ f₂ && boolEq m₁ m₂
  | .aggregateEnum d₁ v₁ os₁, .aggregateEnum d₂ v₂ os₂ =>
    Nat.beq d₁ d₂ && Nat.beq v₁ v₂ && listRel operandEq os₁ os₂
  | .discriminantDirect d₁ s₁, .discriminantDirect d₂ s₂ =>
    Nat.beq d₁ d₂ && Nat.beq s₁ s₂
  | _, _ => false

/-- Terminator in an `EnumBlock`: embeds every unmodified `TerminatorKind` plus
`switchDiscr discrDst enumLocal targets` (modeling `_discrDst = discriminant(_e);
switchInt (move _discrDst) -> targets`, as matched by
`rustc_mir_transform::unreachable_enum_branching`). -/
inductive EnumTerminator where
  | baseTerm (term : TerminatorKind)
  | switchDiscr (discrDst : LocalId) (enumLocal : LocalId)
      (targets : SwitchTargets)

/-- Structural equality on `EnumTerminator`. -/
noncomputable def enumTerminatorEq : EnumTerminator → EnumTerminator → Bool
  | .baseTerm t₁, .baseTerm t₂ => terminatorEq t₁ t₂
  | .switchDiscr d₁ e₁ ts₁, .switchDiscr d₂ e₂ ts₂ =>
    Nat.beq d₁ d₂ && Nat.beq e₁ e₂ && switchTargetsEq ts₁ ts₂
  | _, _ => false

/-- Basic block in `M_enum`. -/
structure EnumBlock where
  statements : List EnumStmt
  terminator : EnumTerminator
  cleanup : Bool := false

/-- Structural equality on `EnumBlock`. -/
noncomputable def enumBlockEq (a b : EnumBlock) : Bool :=
  boolEq a.cleanup b.cleanup &&
    listRel enumStmtEq a.statements b.statements &&
    enumTerminatorEq a.terminator b.terminator

/-- Function body in `M_enum`. -/
structure EnumBody where
  argumentCount : Nat
  locals : List EnumLocalDecl
  basicBlocks : List EnumBlock
  isUnsafe : Bool := false
  identity : String := ""

/-- Structural equality on `EnumBody`. -/
noncomputable def enumBodyEq (a b : EnumBody) : Bool :=
  Nat.beq a.argumentCount b.argumentCount &&
    listRel enumLocalDeclEq a.locals b.locals &&
    listRel enumBlockEq a.basicBlocks b.basicBlocks &&
    boolEq a.isUnsafe b.isUnsafe &&
    stringBeq a.identity b.identity

/-- Complete program in `M_enum`. -/
structure EnumProgram where
  enumDefs : List AdtEnumDef := []
  bodies : List EnumBody
  entryDefId : DefId := 0
  pointerWidthBits : Nat
  mirProfileVersion : Nat
  scope : VerificationScope := .unit

/-- Structural equality on `EnumProgram`. -/
noncomputable def enumProgramEq (a b : EnumProgram) : Bool :=
  listRel adtEnumDefEq a.enumDefs b.enumDefs &&
    listRel enumBodyEq a.bodies b.bodies &&
    Nat.beq a.entryDefId b.entryDefId &&
    Nat.beq a.pointerWidthBits b.pointerWidthBits &&
    Nat.beq a.mirProfileVersion b.mirProfileVersion &&
    scopeEq a.scope b.scope

/-- Embed an unmodified `Trusted.MirAst.BasicBlock` into `EnumBlock`. -/
noncomputable def embedBaseBlock (bb : BasicBlock) : EnumBlock := {
  statements := bb.statements.map EnumStmt.baseStmt
  terminator := .baseTerm bb.terminator
  cleanup := bb.cleanup
}

/-- Embed an unmodified `Trusted.MirAst.Body` into `EnumBody`. -/
noncomputable def embedBaseBody (b : Body) : EnumBody := {
  argumentCount := b.argumentCount
  locals := b.locals.map EnumLocalDecl.base
  basicBlocks := b.basicBlocks.map embedBaseBlock
  isUnsafe := b.isUnsafe
  identity := b.identity
}

/-- Canonical embedding of an unmodified `Trusted.MirAst.Program` into
`EnumProgram`. -/
noncomputable def embedBaseProgram (p : Program) : EnumProgram := {
  enumDefs := []
  bodies := p.bodies.map embedBaseBody
  entryDefId := p.entryDefId
  pointerWidthBits := p.pointerWidthBits
  mirProfileVersion := p.mirProfileVersion
  scope := p.scope
}

/-- Check whether an `EnumProgram` uses strictly unmodified `Trusted.MirAst`
declarations, statements, and terminators (`isBaseEnumProgram`). -/
noncomputable def isBaseEnumBlock (bb : EnumBlock) : Bool :=
  bb.statements.all (fun s => match s with | .baseStmt _ => true | _ => false) &&
    match bb.terminator with | .baseTerm _ => true | _ => false

noncomputable def isBaseEnumBody (b : EnumBody) : Bool :=
  b.locals.all (fun d => match d with | .base _ => true | _ => false) &&
    b.basicBlocks.all isBaseEnumBlock

noncomputable def isBaseEnumProgram (p : EnumProgram) : Bool :=
  p.enumDefs.isEmpty && p.bodies.all isBaseEnumBody

/-- Project a base `EnumProgram` (`isBaseEnumProgram p = true`) back to an
unmodified `Trusted.MirAst.Program`. -/
noncomputable def unembedBaseBlock (bb : EnumBlock) : Option BasicBlock :=
  let stmts? := listMapOption (fun s =>
    match s with | .baseStmt st => some st | _ => none) bb.statements
  match stmts?, bb.terminator with
  | some stmts, .baseTerm t =>
    some { statements := stmts, terminator := t, cleanup := bb.cleanup }
  | _, _ => none

noncomputable def unembedBaseBody (b : EnumBody) : Option Body :=
  let tys? := listMapOption (fun d =>
    match d with | .base ty => some ty | _ => none) b.locals
  let bbs? := listMapOption unembedBaseBlock b.basicBlocks
  match tys?, bbs? with
  | some tys, some bbs =>
    some {
      argumentCount := b.argumentCount
      locals := tys
      basicBlocks := bbs
      isUnsafe := b.isUnsafe
      identity := b.identity
    }
  | _, _ => none

noncomputable def unembedBaseProgram (p : EnumProgram) : Option Program :=
  if !p.enumDefs.isEmpty then
    none
  else
    match listMapOption unembedBaseBody p.bodies with
    | some bs =>
      some {
        bodies := bs
        entryDefId := p.entryDefId
        pointerWidthBits := p.pointerWidthBits
        mirProfileVersion := p.mirProfileVersion
        scope := p.scope
      }
    | none => none

/-! ### Runtime State & Small-Step Transition Rules of `M_enum` -/

/-- Runtime slot state in `M_enum`:
- `.baseSlot s`: exact `Trusted.MirSemantics.LocalSlot` (`dead` or `live optVal`).
- `.enumDead`: dead `AdtEnum` local (`LocalValue::Dead`).
- `.liveEmpty`: live 0-variant `.empty` enum local.
- `.liveSingle fields`: live 1-variant `.single` enum local with per-field
  `Option Val`.
- `.liveDirect tag variantFields`: live `.direct` enum local with optional
  active variant index `tag` (`none` when tag bytes are `Uninit`) and per-variant
  payload fields.
- `.liveNiche nicheBits extraFields`: live `.niche` enum local sharing
  `nicheBits : Option (BitVec 128)` between the niche tag and
  `(_e as untagged).nicheFieldIdx`, plus `extraFields` for `f ≠ nicheFieldIdx`
  of `untaggedVariant`. -/
inductive EnumSlot where
  | baseSlot (slot : LocalSlot)
  | enumDead
  | liveEmpty
  | liveSingle (fields : List (Option Val))
  | liveDirect (tag : Option Nat) (variantFields : List (List (Option Val)))
  | liveNiche (nicheBits : Option (BitVec 128))
      (extraFields : List (Option Val))

/-- Active frame state of `M_enum`. -/
structure EnumFrame where
  defId : DefId
  blockIdx : BasicBlockId
  stmtIdx : Nat
  locals : List EnumSlot

/-- Running machine state of `M_enum`. -/
structure EnumState where
  frames : List EnumFrame
  callerMem : CallerMemory := ⟨[]⟩

/-- Embed an unmodified `Trusted.MirSemantics.State` into `EnumState`. -/
noncomputable def embedEnumFrame (f : FrameState) : EnumFrame := {
  defId := f.defId
  blockIdx := f.blockIdx
  stmtIdx := f.stmtIdx
  locals := f.locals.map EnumSlot.baseSlot
}

noncomputable def embedEnumState (s : State) : EnumState := {
  frames := s.frames.map embedEnumFrame
  callerMem := s.callerMem
}

noncomputable def liftStepResultEnum :
    StepResult State TerminalOut → StepResult EnumState TerminalOut
  | .step s => .step (embedEnumState s)
  | .done o => .done o
  | .fault k => .fault k

/-- Build the `extraFields` list (`f ≠ nicheField`) for `untagged` at
initialization / `StorageLive`. -/
noncomputable def initNicheExtraFieldsAux (nicheField : Nat) :
    Nat → List MirTy → List (Option Val)
  | _, [] => []
  | idx, ty :: rest =>
    if Nat.beq idx nicheField then
      initNicheExtraFieldsAux nicheField (idx + 1) rest
    else
      initFieldOptVal ty :: initNicheExtraFieldsAux nicheField (idx + 1) rest

/-- Initial live uninitialized `EnumSlot` for a local declaration `decl`. -/
noncomputable def liveUninitEnumSlot (enumDefs : List AdtEnumDef) :
    EnumLocalDecl → Option EnumSlot
  | .base ty => some (.baseSlot (liveUninitSlot ty))
  | .adtEnum eIdx =>
    match Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? enumDefs eIdx with
    | none => none
    | some ed =>
      if !adtEnumDefAdmitted ed then
        none
      else
        match ed.layout with
        | .empty => some .liveEmpty
        | .single =>
          match Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? ed.variants 0 with
          | some vd => some (.liveSingle (vd.fields.map initFieldOptVal))
          | none => none
        | .direct _ _ =>
          let vfs := ed.variants.map (fun vd => vd.fields.map initFieldOptVal)
          some (.liveDirect none vfs)
        | .niche _ untagged _ _ _ _ nicheField _ =>
          match Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? ed.variants untagged with
          | some uVd =>
            some (.liveNiche none (initNicheExtraFieldsAux nicheField 0 uVd.fields))
          | none => none

/-- Whether `stmt : EnumStmt` is a `StorageLive` or `StorageDead` marker for
`localId`. -/
noncomputable def enumStmtHasStorageMarker (localId : LocalId) :
    EnumStmt → Bool
  | .baseStmt s => stmtHasStorageMarker localId s
  | _ => false

/-- Whether any block in `body` carries a `StorageLive` or `StorageDead`
annotation for `localId`. -/
noncomputable def enumHasStorageAnnotation (body : EnumBody)
    (localId : LocalId) : Bool :=
  body.basicBlocks.any (fun bb =>
    bb.statements.any (enumStmtHasStorageMarker localId))

/-- Check that every `StorageLive` and `StorageDead` local index in `body` is
in bounds (`< body.locals.length`). -/
noncomputable def enumStorageAnnotationsInBounds (body : EnumBody) : Bool :=
  let n := body.locals.length
  body.basicBlocks.all (fun bb =>
    bb.statements.all (fun stmt =>
      match stmt with
      | .baseStmt (.storageLive id) | .baseStmt (.storageDead id) =>
        Nat.blt id n
      | _ => true))

/-- Check whether `decl : EnumLocalDecl` is statically supported (and for
parameter/return slots `0 .. argumentCount`, we require `.base ty` matching
`Trusted.MirSemantics.Query` / `Out`, while internal locals `> argumentCount`
may be either `.base ty` or an admitted `.adtEnum eIdx`). -/
noncomputable def isSupportedEnumLocalDecl (enumDefs : List AdtEnumDef)
    (argumentCount : Nat) (idx : Nat) : EnumLocalDecl → Bool
  | .base ty => isSupportedScalarOrUnitTy ty
  | .adtEnum eIdx =>
    Nat.blt argumentCount idx &&
      match Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? enumDefs eIdx with
      | some ed => adtEnumDefAdmitted ed
      | none => false

noncomputable def allEnumLocalsSupported (enumDefs : List AdtEnumDef)
    (argumentCount : Nat) : Nat → List EnumLocalDecl → Bool
  | _, [] => true
  | idx, d :: rest =>
    isSupportedEnumLocalDecl enumDefs argumentCount idx d &&
      allEnumLocalsSupported enumDefs argumentCount (idx + 1) rest

/-- Extract parameter `MirTy` list (`1 .. argumentCount`) when all signature
slots are `.base ty`. -/
noncomputable def enumParamBaseTys? (body : EnumBody) : Option (List MirTy) :=
  listMapOption (fun d => match d with | .base ty => some ty | _ => none)
    ((body.locals.drop 1).take body.argumentCount)

/-- Initialize local slots of `body` at entry in `M_enum`. -/
noncomputable def initEnumLocalsLoop (enumDefs : List AdtEnumDef)
    (body : EnumBody) (args : List Val) :
    Nat → List EnumLocalDecl → Option (List EnumSlot)
  | _, [] => some []
  | idx, decl :: rest =>
    let slot? : Option EnumSlot :=
      if Nat.beq idx 0 then
        liveUninitEnumSlot enumDefs decl
      else if Nat.ble idx body.argumentCount then
        match Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? args (idx - 1) with
        | some v => some (.baseSlot (.live (some v)))
        | none => some (.baseSlot .dead)
      else if enumHasStorageAnnotation body idx then
        match decl with
        | .base _ => some (.baseSlot .dead)
        | .adtEnum _ => some .enumDead
      else
        liveUninitEnumSlot enumDefs decl
    match slot?, initEnumLocalsLoop enumDefs body args (idx + 1) rest with
    | some sl, some tail => some (sl :: tail)
    | _, _ => none

/-- Entry initialization `initStateEnum p q` in `M_enum`. -/
noncomputable def initStateEnum (p : EnumProgram) (q : Query) :
    Except FaultKind EnumState :=
  if !Nat.beq p.pointerWidthBits 64 || !Nat.beq p.mirProfileVersion 1 then
    .error .unsupported
  else if !q.callerMem.allocations.isEmpty then
    .error .unsupported
  else if !p.enumDefs.all adtEnumDefAdmitted then
    .error .unsupported
  else
    match Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? p.bodies p.entryDefId with
    | none => .error .unsupported
    | some body =>
      if body.basicBlocks.isEmpty then
        .error .unsupported
      else if !Nat.blt body.argumentCount body.locals.length then
        .error .unsupported
      else if !enumStorageAnnotationsInBounds body then
        .error .unsupported
      else if !allEnumLocalsSupported p.enumDefs body.argumentCount 0 body.locals then
        .error .unsupported
      else
        match enumParamBaseTys? body with
        | none => .error .unsupported
        | some paramTys =>
          if !checkArgsMatch q.args paramTys then
            .error .unsupported
          else
            match initEnumLocalsLoop p.enumDefs body q.args 0 body.locals with
            | none => .error .unsupported
            | some locals =>
              let frame : EnumFrame := {
                defId := p.entryDefId
                blockIdx := 0
                stmtIdx := 0
                locals := locals
              }
              .ok { frames := [frame], callerMem := q.callerMem }

/-- Project `EnumBody.locals` and `EnumFrame.locals` onto base `MirTy` and
`LocalSlot` views (`AdtEnum` slots map to `.unit` / `.dead` in the base view so
base `Operand`/`Rvalue` evaluation never touches `AdtEnum` locals and fails
closed if a base statement references an `AdtEnum` local). -/
noncomputable def stmtMentionsLocalOperand (id : LocalId) : Operand → Bool
  | .copy p | .move p => Nat.beq p.localId id
  | .constant _ => false

noncomputable def rvalueMentionsLocal (id : LocalId) : Rvalue → Bool
  | .use o | .unaryOp _ o => stmtMentionsLocalOperand id o
  | .binaryOp _ l r => stmtMentionsLocalOperand id l || stmtMentionsLocalOperand id r
  | .discriminant p | .ref _ p | .addressOf _ p => Nat.beq p.localId id
  | .aggregateTuple os => os.any (stmtMentionsLocalOperand id)
  | .unsupported => false

/-- Evaluate a base `Operand` over `EnumBody.locals` and `EnumFrame.locals`
without reconstructing lists when no `.adtEnum` local is referenced. -/
noncomputable def evalEnumBaseOperandToSlot (decls : List EnumLocalDecl)
    (slots : List EnumSlot) :
    Operand → Except FaultKind (MirTy × Option Val × List EnumSlot)
  | .copy place =>
    if !place.projection.isEmpty then
      .error .unsupported
    else
      match Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? decls place.localId, Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? slots place.localId with
      | some (.base ty), some (.baseSlot (.live optVal)) =>
        .ok (ty, optVal, slots)
      | some (.base _), some (.baseSlot .dead) =>
        .error .undefined
      | _, _ => .error .unsupported
  | .move place =>
    if !place.projection.isEmpty then
      .error .unsupported
    else
      match Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? decls place.localId, Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? slots place.localId with
      | some (.base ty), some (.baseSlot (.live optVal)) =>
        match setElem? slots place.localId (.baseSlot (liveUninitSlot ty)) with
        | some slots' => .ok (ty, optVal, slots')
        | none => .error .unsupported
      | some (.base _), some (.baseSlot .dead) =>
        .error .undefined
      | _, _ => .error .unsupported
  | .constant c =>
    match evalConstLit c.ty c.lit with
    | .ok v => .ok (c.ty, some v, slots)
    | .error k => .error k

noncomputable def evalEnumPrimitiveOperand (decls : List EnumLocalDecl)
    (slots : List EnumSlot) (opnd : Operand) :
    Except FaultKind (Val × List EnumSlot) :=
  match evalEnumBaseOperandToSlot decls slots opnd with
  | .error k => .error k
  | .ok (ty, optVal, slots') =>
    if !isPrimitiveReadableTy ty then
      .error .unsupported
    else
      match optVal with
      | some v => .ok (v, slots')
      | none => .error .undefined

/-- Evaluate a base `Rvalue` over `EnumLocalDecl` / `EnumSlot` lists in exact
1-to-1 lockstep with `Trusted.MirSemantics.evalRvalue`. -/
noncomputable def evalEnumBaseRvalue (decls : List EnumLocalDecl)
    (slots : List EnumSlot) (dstTy : MirTy) :
    Rvalue → Except FaultKind (Val × List EnumSlot)
  | .use opnd =>
    match evalEnumBaseOperandToSlot decls slots opnd with
    | .error k => .error k
    | .ok (srcTy, optVal, slots₁) =>
      if !(MirTy.beq srcTy dstTy) then
        .error .unsupported
      else
        match optVal with
        | some v => .ok (v, slots₁)
        | none => .error .undefined
  | .binaryOp op lhs rhs =>
    match evalEnumPrimitiveOperand decls slots lhs with
    | .error k => .error k
    | .ok (lVal, slots₁) =>
      match evalEnumPrimitiveOperand decls slots₁ rhs with
      | .error k => .error k
      | .ok (rVal, slots₂) =>
        match evalBinOp op lVal rVal with
        | .error k => .error k
        | .ok res => .ok (res, slots₂)
  | .unaryOp op opnd =>
    match evalEnumPrimitiveOperand decls slots opnd with
    | .error k => .error k
    | .ok (v, slots₁) =>
      match evalUnOp op v with
      | .error k => .error k
      | .ok res => .ok (res, slots₁)
  | .discriminant place =>
    if !place.projection.isEmpty then
      .error .unsupported
    else
      match Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? decls place.localId, Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? slots place.localId with
      | some (.base (.enum ety)), some (.baseSlot slot) =>
        if !enumAdmitted ety then
          .error .unsupported
        else
          match ety.tagRepr, slot with
          | _, .dead => .error .undefined
          | .zeroSized, .live none =>
            match Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? ety.discriminants 0 with
            | some disc =>
              .ok (.scalar ⟨ety.discrWidth, ety.discrSigned,
                truncateBits ety.discrWidth (BitVec.ofNat 128 disc)⟩, slots)
            | none => .error .unsupported
          | .zeroSized, .live (some (.enumVal ety' v)) =>
            if EnumTy.beq ety ety' && Nat.beq v 0 then
              match Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? ety.discriminants 0 with
              | some disc =>
                .ok (.scalar ⟨ety.discrWidth, ety.discrSigned,
                  truncateBits ety.discrWidth (BitVec.ofNat 128 disc)⟩, slots)
              | none => .error .unsupported
            else
              .error .unsupported
          | .zeroSized, .live (some _) => .error .unsupported
          | .scalar _ _, .live none => .error .undefined
          | .scalar _ _, .live (some (.enumVal ety' v)) =>
            if EnumTy.beq ety ety' && Nat.blt v ety.discriminants.length then
              match Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? ety.discriminants v with
              | some disc =>
                .ok (.scalar ⟨ety.discrWidth, ety.discrSigned,
                  truncateBits ety.discrWidth (BitVec.ofNat 128 disc)⟩, slots)
              | none => .error .unsupported
            else
              .error .unsupported
          | .scalar _ _, .live (some _) => .error .unsupported
      | _, _ => .error .unsupported
  | _ => .error .unsupported

/-- Write `val` into an unprojected `.base dstTy` local slot in `slots`, matching
`Trusted.MirSemantics.writePlace`. -/
noncomputable def writeEnumBasePlace (slots : List EnumSlot)
    (dstLocalId : LocalId) (dstTy : MirTy) (val : Val) :
    Except FaultKind (List EnumSlot) :=
  if !checkVal val dstTy then
    .error .unsupported
  else
    match Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? slots dstLocalId with
    | none => .error .unsupported
    | some (.baseSlot .dead) => .error .undefined
    | some (.baseSlot (.live _)) =>
      match setElem? slots dstLocalId (.baseSlot (.live (some val))) with
      | some slots' => .ok slots'
      | none => .error .unsupported
    | some _ => .error .unsupported

/-- Decode active variant index from a `.niche` enum's `nicheBits`, matching
`Miri.Interpreter.Discriminant.readDiscriminant`
(`vendor/lean-miri/Miri/Interpreter/Discriminant.lean:127-156`). -/
noncomputable def decodeNicheVariant (ed : AdtEnumDef)
    (tagW : IntWidth) (untagged nStart nLast : Nat)
    (nStartBits : BitVec 128) (tagRange : WrappingRange128) :
    Option (BitVec 128) → Except FaultKind Nat
  | none => .error .undefined
  | some bits =>
    if truncateBits tagW bits != bits then
      .error .unsupported
    else if !wrappingRangeContains tagRange bits then
      .error .undefined
    else
      let rel := subTruncBits tagW bits nStartBits
      let span := nLast - nStart
      let idx :=
        if Nat.ble rel.toNat span then
          nStart + rel.toNat
        else
          untagged
      match Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? ed.variants idx with
      | none => .error .unsupported
      | some vd =>
        if variantIsUninhabited vd then
          .error .undefined
        else
          .ok idx

/-- Read the declared `Ty::discriminant_ty` scalar of an `AdtEnum` slot,
matching `Miri.Interpreter.Discriminant.readDiscriminant`
(`vendor/lean-miri/Miri/Interpreter/Discriminant.lean:94-156`). -/
noncomputable def readAdtDiscriminant (ed : AdtEnumDef) (slot : EnumSlot) :
    Except FaultKind Val :=
  if !adtEnumDefAdmitted ed then
    .error .unsupported
  else
    match ed.layout, slot with
    | _, .enumDead => .error .undefined
    | .empty, .liveEmpty => .error .undefined
    | .single, .liveSingle _ =>
      match Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? ed.variants 0 with
      | none => .error .unsupported
      | some vd =>
        if variantIsUninhabited vd then
          .error .undefined
        else
          .ok (.scalar ⟨ed.discrWidth, ed.discrSigned,
            truncateBits ed.discrWidth (BitVec.ofNat 128 vd.discrVal)⟩)
    | .direct _ _, .liveDirect none _ => .error .undefined
    | .direct _ _, .liveDirect (some v) _ =>
      match Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? ed.variants v with
      | none => .error .unsupported
      | some vd =>
        if variantIsUninhabited vd then
          .error .undefined
        else
          .ok (.scalar ⟨ed.discrWidth, ed.discrSigned,
            truncateBits ed.discrWidth (BitVec.ofNat 128 vd.discrVal)⟩)
    | .niche tagW untagged nStart nLast nStartBits tagRange _ _,
      .liveNiche nicheBits _ =>
      match decodeNicheVariant ed tagW untagged nStart nLast nStartBits tagRange nicheBits with
      | .error k => .error k
      | .ok v =>
        match Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? ed.variants v with
        | none => .error .unsupported
        | some vd =>
          .ok (.scalar ⟨ed.discrWidth, ed.discrSigned,
            truncateBits ed.discrWidth (BitVec.ofNat 128 vd.discrVal)⟩)
    | _, _ => .error .unsupported

/-- Execute `StatementKind::SetDiscriminant` (`writeDiscriminant` in
`vendor/lean-miri/Miri/Interpreter/Discriminant.lean:158-168`):
- Checks `v < ed.variants.length` (else `.error .unsupported`) and `slot != .enumDead`
  (else `.error .undefined`).
- Checks `!variantIsUninhabited vd` (else `.error .undefined`,
  `UninhabitedEnumVariantWritten`).
- On `.niche`: if `v` is a niche variant (`v ∈ [nStart, nLast]`), writes the
  niche bit pattern `(v - nStart + nStartBits) mod 2^tagW` into `nicheBits`; if
  `v == untagged`, calls `decodeNicheVariant` on `nicheBits` and faults
  `.error .undefined` (`InvalidNichedEnumVariantWritten` / `InvalidUninitBytes`)
  unless `actual == untagged`! -/
noncomputable def writeAdtDiscriminant (ed : AdtEnumDef) (v : Nat)
    (slot : EnumSlot) : Except FaultKind EnumSlot :=
  if !adtEnumDefAdmitted ed then
    .error .unsupported
  else
    match Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? ed.variants v with
    | none => .error .unsupported
    | some vd =>
      match slot with
      | .enumDead => .error .undefined
      | .baseSlot _ => .error .unsupported
      | _ =>
        if variantIsUninhabited vd then
          .error .undefined
        else
          match ed.layout, slot with
          | .empty, _ => .error .unsupported
          | .single, .liveSingle fs =>
            if Nat.beq v 0 then .ok (.liveSingle fs) else .error .unsupported
          | .direct _ _, .liveDirect _ vfs =>
            .ok (.liveDirect (some v) vfs)
          | .niche tagW untagged nStart nLast nStartBits tagRange _ _,
            .liveNiche nicheBits extras =>
            if Nat.beq v untagged then
              match decodeNicheVariant ed tagW untagged nStart nLast nStartBits tagRange nicheBits with
              | .error k => .error k
              | .ok actual =>
                if Nat.beq actual untagged then
                  .ok (.liveNiche nicheBits extras)
                else
                  .error .undefined
            else if Nat.ble nStart v && Nat.ble v nLast then
              let tagBits :=
                addTruncBits tagW (BitVec.ofNat 128 (v - nStart)) nStartBits
              .ok (.liveNiche (some tagBits) extras)
            else
              .error .unsupported
          | _, _ => .error .unsupported

/-- Compute the compact `extraFields` index for `f ≠ nicheField` in a `.niche`
`untagged` variant: `f` if `f < nicheField`, `f - 1` if `f > nicheField`. -/
noncomputable def nicheExtraIdx (nicheField f : Nat) : Nat :=
  if Nat.blt f nicheField then f else f - 1

/-- Write `val` into `(_e as Variant#v).f` (`assignField`). -/
noncomputable def writeAdtField (ed : AdtEnumDef) (v f : Nat) (fTy : MirTy)
    (val : Val) (slot : EnumSlot) : Except FaultKind EnumSlot :=
  if !adtEnumDefAdmitted ed || !checkVal val fTy then
    .error .unsupported
  else
    match slot with
    | .enumDead => .error .undefined
    | .liveSingle fs =>
      if !Nat.beq v 0 then
        .error .unsupported
      else
        match setElem? fs f (some val) with
        | some fs' => .ok (.liveSingle fs')
        | none => .error .unsupported
    | .liveDirect tag vfs =>
      match Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? vfs v with
      | none => .error .unsupported
      | some fs =>
        match setElem? fs f (some val) with
        | none => .error .unsupported
        | some fs' =>
          match setElem? vfs v fs' with
          | some vfs' => .ok (.liveDirect tag vfs')
          | none => .error .unsupported
    | .liveNiche nicheBits extras =>
      match ed.layout with
      | .niche tagW untagged nStart nLast _ _ nicheField uRange =>
        if Nat.beq v untagged then
          if Nat.beq f nicheField then
            match val with
            | .scalar sv =>
              if !(IntWidth.beq sv.width tagW && !sv.signed && sv.wf) then
                .error .unsupported
              else if !wrappingRangeContains uRange sv.bits then
                .error .undefined
              else
                .ok (.liveNiche (some sv.bits) extras)
            | _ => .error .unsupported
          else
            match setElem? extras (nicheExtraIdx nicheField f) (some val) with
            | some extras' => .ok (.liveNiche nicheBits extras')
            | none => .error .unsupported
        else if Nat.ble nStart v && Nat.ble v nLast then
          -- Niche variants carry only ZST fields (`isZstBaseTy fTy`).
          if isZstBaseTy fTy then
            .ok (.liveNiche nicheBits extras)
          else
            .error .unsupported
        else
          .error .unsupported
      | _ => .error .unsupported
    | _ => .error .unsupported

/-- Read `copy` or `move` from `(_e as Variant#v).f` (`readField`). -/
noncomputable def readAdtField (ed : AdtEnumDef) (v f : Nat) (fTy : MirTy)
    (isMove : Bool) (slot : EnumSlot) : Except FaultKind (Val × EnumSlot) :=
  if !adtEnumDefAdmitted ed then
    .error .unsupported
  else
    match slot with
    | .enumDead => .error .undefined
    | .liveSingle fs =>
      if !Nat.beq v 0 then
        .error .unsupported
      else
        match Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? fs f with
        | none => .error .unsupported
        | some none => .error .undefined
        | some (some val) =>
          if !isMove then
            .ok (val, .liveSingle fs)
          else
            match setElem? fs f (initFieldOptVal fTy) with
            | some fs' => .ok (val, .liveSingle fs')
            | none => .error .unsupported
    | .liveDirect tag vfs =>
      match Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? vfs v with
      | none => .error .unsupported
      | some fs =>
        match Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? fs f with
        | none => .error .unsupported
        | some none => .error .undefined
        | some (some val) =>
          if !isMove then
            .ok (val, .liveDirect tag vfs)
          else
            match setElem? fs f (initFieldOptVal fTy) with
            | none => .error .unsupported
            | some fs' =>
              match setElem? vfs v fs' with
              | some vfs' => .ok (val, .liveDirect tag vfs')
              | none => .error .unsupported
    | .liveNiche nicheBits extras =>
      match ed.layout with
      | .niche tagW untagged nStart nLast _ _ nicheField uRange =>
        if Nat.beq v untagged then
          if Nat.beq f nicheField then
            match nicheBits with
            | none => .error .undefined
            | some bits =>
              if truncateBits tagW bits != bits then
                .error .unsupported
              else if !wrappingRangeContains uRange bits then
                .error .undefined
              else
                let val : Val := .scalar ⟨tagW, false, bits⟩
                let nextBits := if isMove then none else some bits
                .ok (val, .liveNiche nextBits extras)
          else
            let eIdx := nicheExtraIdx nicheField f
            match Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? extras eIdx with
            | none => .error .unsupported
            | some none => .error .undefined
            | some (some val) =>
              if !isMove then
                .ok (val, .liveNiche nicheBits extras)
              else
                match setElem? extras eIdx (initFieldOptVal fTy) with
                | some extras' => .ok (val, .liveNiche nicheBits extras')
                | none => .error .unsupported
        else if Nat.ble nStart v && Nat.ble v nLast then
          match initFieldOptVal fTy with
          | some zVal => .ok (zVal, .liveNiche nicheBits extras)
          | none => .error .unsupported
        else
          .error .unsupported
      | _ => .error .unsupported
    | _ => .error .unsupported

/-- Evaluate a list of `Operand`s left-to-right against typed `VariantDef.fields`
for `AggregateEnum`. -/
noncomputable def evalAggregateEnumOperands (decls : List EnumLocalDecl)
    (slots : List EnumSlot) :
    List Operand → List MirTy → Except FaultKind (List Val × List EnumSlot)
  | [], [] => .ok ([], slots)
  | op :: ops, ty :: tys =>
    match evalEnumBaseOperandToSlot decls slots op with
    | .error k => .error k
    | .ok (srcTy, optVal, slots₁) =>
      if !(MirTy.beq srcTy ty) then
        .error .unsupported
      else
        match optVal with
        | none => .error .undefined
        | some v =>
          if !checkVal v ty then
            .error .unsupported
          else
            match evalAggregateEnumOperands decls slots₁ ops tys with
            | .error k => .error k
            | .ok (vs, slots₂) => .ok (v :: vs, slots₂)
  | _, _ => .error .unsupported

/-- Write payload values `vals` into variant `v` of `slot` left-to-right, then
apply `writeAdtDiscriminant ed v`. -/
noncomputable def writeAdtFieldsSeq (ed : AdtEnumDef) (v idx : Nat) :
    List MirTy → List Val → EnumSlot → Except FaultKind EnumSlot
  | [], [], slot => .ok slot
  | fTy :: fTys, val :: vals, slot =>
    match writeAdtField ed v idx fTy val slot with
    | .error k => .error k
    | .ok slot₁ => writeAdtFieldsSeq ed v (idx + 1) fTys vals slot₁
  | _, _, _ => .error .unsupported

/-- Evaluate a single `EnumStmt` in `M_enum`. -/
noncomputable def evalEnumStmt (enumDefs : List AdtEnumDef) (body : EnumBody)
    (frame : EnumFrame) (callerMem : CallerMemory) (stmt : EnumStmt) :
    StepResult EnumState TerminalOut :=
  match stmt with
  | .baseStmt .nop =>
    .step { frames := [{ frame with stmtIdx := frame.stmtIdx + 1 }], callerMem }
  | .baseStmt (.storageLive localId) =>
    match Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? body.locals localId with
    | none => .fault .unsupported
    | some decl =>
      match liveUninitEnumSlot enumDefs decl with
      | none => .fault .unsupported
      | some initSl =>
        match setElem? frame.locals localId initSl with
        | some slots' =>
          .step {
            frames := [{ frame with stmtIdx := frame.stmtIdx + 1, locals := slots' }]
            callerMem
          }
        | none => .fault .unsupported
  | .baseStmt (.storageDead localId) =>
    if Nat.beq localId 0 then
      .fault .unsupported
    else
      let deadSl : EnumSlot :=
        match Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? body.locals localId with
        | some (.adtEnum _) => .enumDead
        | _ => .baseSlot .dead
      match setElem? frame.locals localId deadSl with
      | some slots' =>
        .step {
          frames := [{ frame with stmtIdx := frame.stmtIdx + 1, locals := slots' }]
          callerMem
        }
      | none => .fault .unsupported
  | .baseStmt (.assign dst rvalue) =>
    if !dst.projection.isEmpty then
      .fault .unsupported
    else
      match Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? body.locals dst.localId with
      | some (.base dstTy) =>
        match evalEnumBaseRvalue body.locals frame.locals dstTy rvalue with
        | .error k => .fault k
        | .ok (val, slotsAfterRval) =>
          match writeEnumBasePlace slotsAfterRval dst.localId dstTy val with
          | .error k => .fault k
          | .ok slotsAfterWrite =>
            .step {
              frames := [{
                frame with
                stmtIdx := frame.stmtIdx + 1
                locals := slotsAfterWrite
              }]
              callerMem
            }
      | _ => .fault .unsupported
  | .baseStmt .unsupported =>
    .fault .unsupported
  | .setDiscriminant localId variantIdx =>
    match Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? body.locals localId, Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? frame.locals localId with
    | some (.adtEnum eIdx), some sl =>
      match Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? enumDefs eIdx with
      | none => .fault .unsupported
      | some ed =>
        match writeAdtDiscriminant ed variantIdx sl with
        | .error k => .fault k
        | .ok sl' =>
          match setElem? frame.locals localId sl' with
          | some slots' =>
            .step {
              frames := [{ frame with stmtIdx := frame.stmtIdx + 1, locals := slots' }]
              callerMem
            }
          | none => .fault .unsupported
    | _, _ => .fault .unsupported
  | .assignField localId variantIdx fieldIdx rval =>
    if rvalueMentionsLocal localId rval then
      .fault .unsupported
    else
      match Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? body.locals localId with
      | some (.adtEnum eIdx) =>
        match Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? enumDefs eIdx with
        | none => .fault .unsupported
        | some ed =>
          match Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? ed.variants variantIdx with
          | none => .fault .unsupported
          | some vd =>
            match Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? vd.fields fieldIdx with
            | none => .fault .unsupported
            | some fTy =>
              match evalEnumBaseRvalue body.locals frame.locals fTy rval with
              | .error k => .fault k
              | .ok (val, slotsAfterRval) =>
                match Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? slotsAfterRval localId with
                | none => .fault .unsupported
                | some sl =>
                  match writeAdtField ed variantIdx fieldIdx fTy val sl with
                  | .error k => .fault k
                  | .ok sl' =>
                    match setElem? slotsAfterRval localId sl' with
                    | some slots' =>
                      .step {
                        frames := [{
                          frame with
                          stmtIdx := frame.stmtIdx + 1
                          locals := slots'
                        }]
                        callerMem
                      }
                    | none => .fault .unsupported
      | _ => .fault .unsupported
  | .readField dstLocal srcLocal variantIdx fieldIdx isMove =>
    if Nat.beq dstLocal srcLocal then
      .fault .unsupported
    else
      match Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? body.locals dstLocal, Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? body.locals srcLocal,
          Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? frame.locals srcLocal with
      | some (.base dstTy), some (.adtEnum eIdx), some sl =>
        match Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? enumDefs eIdx with
        | none => .fault .unsupported
        | some ed =>
          match Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? ed.variants variantIdx with
          | none => .fault .unsupported
          | some vd =>
            match Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? vd.fields fieldIdx with
            | none => .fault .unsupported
            | some fTy =>
              if !(MirTy.beq fTy dstTy) then
                .fault .unsupported
              else
                match readAdtField ed variantIdx fieldIdx fTy isMove sl with
                | .error k => .fault k
                | .ok (val, sl') =>
                  match setElem? frame.locals srcLocal sl' with
                  | none => .fault .unsupported
                  | some slots₁ =>
                    match writeEnumBasePlace slots₁ dstLocal dstTy val with
                    | .error k => .fault k
                    | .ok slots₂ =>
                      .step {
                        frames := [{
                          frame with
                          stmtIdx := frame.stmtIdx + 1
                          locals := slots₂
                        }]
                        callerMem
                      }
      | _, _, _ => .fault .unsupported
  | .aggregateEnum dstLocal variantIdx ops =>
    if ops.any (stmtMentionsLocalOperand dstLocal) then
      .fault .unsupported
    else
      match Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? body.locals dstLocal with
      | some (.adtEnum eIdx) =>
        match Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? enumDefs eIdx with
        | none => .fault .unsupported
        | some ed =>
          if !adtEnumDefAdmitted ed then
            .fault .unsupported
          else
            match Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? ed.variants variantIdx with
            | none => .fault .unsupported
            | some vd =>
              match evalAggregateEnumOperands body.locals frame.locals ops vd.fields with
              | .error k => .fault k
              | .ok (vals, slots₁) =>
                match Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? slots₁ dstLocal with
                | none => .fault .unsupported
                | some .enumDead => .fault .undefined
                | some sl =>
                  if variantIsUninhabited vd then
                    .fault .undefined
                  else
                    match writeAdtFieldsSeq ed variantIdx 0 vd.fields vals sl with
                    | .error k => .fault k
                    | .ok sl₁ =>
                      match writeAdtDiscriminant ed variantIdx sl₁ with
                      | .error k => .fault k
                      | .ok sl₂ =>
                        match setElem? slots₁ dstLocal sl₂ with
                        | some slots₂ =>
                          .step {
                            frames := [{
                              frame with
                              stmtIdx := frame.stmtIdx + 1
                              locals := slots₂
                            }]
                            callerMem
                          }
                        | none => .fault .unsupported
      | _ => .fault .unsupported
  | .discriminantDirect dstLocal srcLocal =>
    match Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? body.locals dstLocal, Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? body.locals srcLocal,
        Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? frame.locals srcLocal with
    | some (.base dstTy), some (.adtEnum eIdx), some sl =>
      match Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? enumDefs eIdx with
      | none => .fault .unsupported
      | some ed =>
        let expectedTy : MirTy := .int ed.discrWidth ed.discrSigned
        if !(MirTy.beq dstTy expectedTy) then
          .fault .unsupported
        else
          match ed.layout with
          | .niche _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ =>
            -- Niche discriminant switching uses `EnumTerminator.switchDiscr`.
            .fault .unsupported
          | _ =>
            match readAdtDiscriminant ed sl with
            | .error k => .fault k
            | .ok discVal =>
              match writeEnumBasePlace frame.locals dstLocal dstTy discVal with
              | .error k => .fault k
              | .ok slots' =>
                .step {
                  frames := [{
                    frame with
                    stmtIdx := frame.stmtIdx + 1
                    locals := slots'
                  }]
                  callerMem
                }
    | _, _, _ => .fault .unsupported

/-- Jump to `(target, 0)` in `M_enum`. -/
noncomputable def jumpToEnumBlock (frame : EnumFrame) (callerMem : CallerMemory)
    (target : BasicBlockId) : StepResult EnumState TerminalOut :=
  .step {
    frames := [{ frame with blockIdx := target, stmtIdx := 0 }]
    callerMem
  }

/-- Evaluate an `EnumTerminator` when `frame.stmtIdx == bb.statements.length`. -/
noncomputable def evalEnumTerminator (enumDefs : List AdtEnumDef)
    (body : EnumBody) (bb : EnumBlock) (frame : EnumFrame)
    (callerMem : CallerMemory) : StepResult EnumState TerminalOut :=
  match bb.terminator with
  | .baseTerm (.goto target) => jumpToEnumBlock frame callerMem target
  | .baseTerm .return_ =>
    if bb.cleanup then
      .fault .unsupported
    else
      match Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? frame.locals 0 with
      | some (.baseSlot (.live (some retVal))) =>
        .done (.returned ⟨retVal, callerMem⟩)
      | some (.baseSlot (.live none)) | some (.baseSlot .dead) | some .enumDead =>
        .fault .undefined
      | _ => .fault .unsupported
  | .baseTerm .unreachable => .fault .undefined
  | .baseTerm (.switchInt discr targets) =>
    match evalEnumPrimitiveOperand body.locals frame.locals discr with
    | .error k => .fault k
    | .ok (discrVal, slotsAfterDiscr) =>
      let targetRes : Except FaultKind BasicBlockId :=
        match discrVal with
        | .scalar sv =>
          evalSwitchBranches sv.width sv.bits targets.otherwise targets.branches
        | .bool b =>
          evalBoolSwitchBranches b targets.otherwise targets.branches
        | _ => .error .unsupported
      match targetRes with
      | .error k => .fault k
      | .ok target =>
        jumpToEnumBlock { frame with locals := slotsAfterDiscr } callerMem target
  | .baseTerm .unwindResume
  | .baseTerm (.assert _ _ _ _ _)
  | .baseTerm (.call _ _ _ _ _)
  | .baseTerm .unsupported =>
    .fault .unsupported
  | .switchDiscr discrDst enumLocal targets =>
    match Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? body.locals discrDst, Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? body.locals enumLocal,
        Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? frame.locals enumLocal with
    | some (.base dstTy), some (.adtEnum eIdx), some sl =>
      match Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? enumDefs eIdx with
      | none => .fault .unsupported
      | some ed =>
        let expectedTy : MirTy := .int ed.discrWidth ed.discrSigned
        if !(MirTy.beq dstTy expectedTy) then
          .fault .unsupported
        else
          match readAdtDiscriminant ed sl with
          | .error k => .fault k
          | .ok discVal =>
            match writeEnumBasePlace frame.locals discrDst dstTy discVal with
            | .error k => .fault k
            | .ok slotsAfterWrite =>
              match discVal with
              | .scalar sv =>
                match evalSwitchBranches sv.width sv.bits targets.otherwise targets.branches with
                | .error k => .fault k
                | .ok target =>
                  jumpToEnumBlock { frame with locals := slotsAfterWrite } callerMem target
              | _ => .fault .unsupported
    | _, _, _ => .fault .unsupported

/-- Total single-step evaluator `evalStepEnum` of `M_enum`. -/
noncomputable def evalStepEnum (p : EnumProgram) (_c : Choice) (s : EnumState) :
    StepResult EnumState TerminalOut :=
  match s.frames with
  | [frame] =>
    match Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? p.bodies frame.defId with
    | none => .fault .unsupported
    | some body =>
      match Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? body.basicBlocks frame.blockIdx with
      | none => .fault .unsupported
      | some bb =>
        match Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? bb.statements frame.stmtIdx with
        | some stmt => evalEnumStmt p.enumDefs body frame s.callerMem stmt
        | none =>
          if Nat.beq frame.stmtIdx bb.statements.length then
            evalEnumTerminator p.enumDefs body bb frame s.callerMem
          else
            .fault .unsupported
  | _ => .fault .unsupported

/-! ### Top-Level Execution & Verification Judgments of `M_enum` -/

noncomputable def ValidChoiceEnum (_p : EnumProgram) (_s : EnumState)
    (c : Choice) : Prop :=
  c = 0

noncomputable def StepEnum (p : EnumProgram) (s : EnumState)
    (res : StepResult EnumState TerminalOut) : Prop :=
  ∃ c : Choice, ValidChoiceEnum p s c ∧ evalStepEnum p c s = res

inductive ReachesEnum (p : EnumProgram) : EnumState → EnumState → Prop where
  | refl (s : EnumState) : ReachesEnum p s s
  | tail {s₁ s₂ s₃ : EnumState} :
      ReachesEnum p s₁ s₂ →
      StepEnum p s₂ (.step s₃) →
      ReachesEnum p s₁ s₃

noncomputable def ReachesResultEnum (p : EnumProgram) (q : Query)
    (res : StepResult EnumState TerminalOut) : Prop :=
  match initStateEnum p q with
  | .error k => res = .fault k
  | .ok s₀ => ∃ s : EnumState, ReachesEnum p s₀ s ∧ StepEnum p s res

noncomputable def WellFormedEnum (p : EnumProgram) (q : Query) : Prop :=
  (∃ s₀ : EnumState, initStateEnum p q = .ok s₀ ∧
    ∀ s : EnumState, ReachesEnum p s₀ s → ∃ c : Choice, ValidChoiceEnum p s c) ∧
  (∀ k : FaultKind, ¬ ReachesResultEnum p q (.fault k))

noncomputable def BehaviorEnum (p : EnumProgram) (q : Query)
    (out : TerminalOut) : Prop :=
  ReachesResultEnum p q (.done out)

/-- Constructive deterministic bounded-fuel step chain for `DivergesEnum`. -/
noncomputable def stepChainFromEnum (p : EnumProgram) :
    Nat → EnumState → Option EnumState
  | 0, s => some s
  | n + 1, s =>
    match evalStepEnum p 0 s with
    | .step s' => stepChainFromEnum p n s'
    | _ => none

noncomputable def DivergesEnum (p : EnumProgram) (q : Query) : Prop :=
  ∃ s₀ : EnumState, initStateEnum p q = .ok s₀ ∧
    ∀ n : Nat, ∃ sₙ : EnumState, stepChainFromEnum p n s₀ = some sₙ

noncomputable def SatisfiesPostEnum (p : EnumProgram) (q : Query)
    (post : TerminalOut → Prop) : Prop :=
  WellFormedEnum p q ∧ ∀ out : TerminalOut, BehaviorEnum p q out → post out

/-- Full bidirectional program equivalence in `M_enum`. -/
noncomputable def FullSemanticEquivEnum (p₁ p₂ : EnumProgram) : Prop :=
  (∀ q : Query, WellFormedEnum p₁ q ↔ WellFormedEnum p₂ q) ∧
  (∀ q : Query, ∀ out : TerminalOut,
    BehaviorEnum p₁ q out ↔ BehaviorEnum p₂ q out) ∧
  (∀ q : Query, ∀ k : FaultKind,
    ReachesResultEnum p₁ q (.fault k) ↔ ReachesResultEnum p₂ q (.fault k)) ∧
  (∀ q : Query, DivergesEnum p₁ q ↔ DivergesEnum p₂ q) ∧
  (∀ q : Query, ∀ post : TerminalOut → Prop,
    SatisfiesPostEnum p₁ q post ↔ SatisfiesPostEnum p₂ q post)

/-- Full bidirectional semantic equivalence on unmodified `Trusted.MirAst.Program`
in `Trusted.MirSemantics` (matching downstream passes `F1-5`..`F1-13`). -/
noncomputable def FullSemanticEquivBase (p₁ p₂ : Program) : Prop :=
  (∀ q : Query, WellFormed p₁ q ↔ WellFormed p₂ q) ∧
  (∀ q : Query, ∀ out : TerminalOut, Behavior p₁ q out ↔ Behavior p₂ q out) ∧
  (∀ q : Query, ∀ k : FaultKind,
    ReachesResult p₁ q (.fault k) ↔ ReachesResult p₂ q (.fault k)) ∧
  (∀ q : Query, Diverges p₁ q ↔ Diverges p₂ q) ∧
  (∀ q : Query, ∀ post : TerminalOut → Prop,
    SatisfiesPost p₁ q post ↔ SatisfiesPost p₂ q post)

/-! ## Part II: Certified `UnreachableEnumBranching` & `EnumScalarize` Lowering -/

/-! ### Pass A: `UnreachableEnumBranching` (`rustc_mir_transform::unreachable_enum_branching`) -/

/-- Collect the truncated `BitVec 128` discriminants of all *inhabited* variants
of `ed : AdtEnumDef`, matching `variant_discriminants` in
`compiler/rustc_mir_transform/src/unreachable_enum_branching.rs:52-78`
(tightened uniformly across `.empty`, `.single`, and `.multiple` so uninhabited
`.single` variants are also pruned). -/
noncomputable def inhabitedDiscrSet : IntWidth → List VariantDef → List (BitVec 128)
  | _, [] => []
  | discrW, vd :: rest =>
    let tail := inhabitedDiscrSet discrW rest
    if variantIsUninhabited vd then
      tail
    else
      truncateBits discrW (BitVec.ofNat 128 vd.discrVal) :: tail

/-- Remove `x` from a `List (BitVec 128)` if present, returning `(wasPresent, remaining)`. -/
noncomputable def removeBitVecOnce (x : BitVec 128) :
    List (BitVec 128) → Bool × List (BitVec 128)
  | [] => (false, [])
  | y :: ys =>
    if x == y then
      (true, ys)
    else
      let res := removeBitVecOnce x ys
      (res.1, y :: res.2)

/-- Rewrite `SwitchTargets.branches` against remaining `allowed` inhabited
discriminants: any branch whose `caseBits` fits `discrW` and is NOT in `allowed`
(either uninhabited, undeclared, or a duplicate of an earlier branch!) has its
target redirected to `unreachBb`, while keeping `caseBits` unchanged (preserving
overflow checks in `evalSwitchBranches`!). -/
noncomputable def pruneEnumBranches (discrW : IntWidth) (unreachBb : BasicBlockId) :
    List (BitVec 128) → List (BitVec 128 × BasicBlockId) →
      List (BitVec 128) × List (BitVec 128 × BasicBlockId)
  | allowed, [] => (allowed, [])
  | allowed, (caseBits, target) :: rest =>
    if truncateBits discrW caseBits != caseBits then
      -- Malformed overflowing case constant: preserve verbatim so
      -- `evalSwitchBranches` still faults `.unsupported` if reached.
      let tail := pruneEnumBranches discrW unreachBb allowed rest
      (tail.1, (caseBits, target) :: tail.2)
    else
      let rem := removeBitVecOnce caseBits allowed
      let tgt' := if rem.1 then target else unreachBb
      let tail := pruneEnumBranches discrW unreachBb rem.2 rest
      (tail.1, (caseBits, tgt') :: tail.2)

/-- Check that every branch constant in `branches` fits unsigned in `discrW`
(`truncateBits discrW caseBits == caseBits`), required before promoting a
trailing arm after `branches` so no earlier malformed case can be skipped or
newly exposed. -/
noncomputable def allSwitchCasesFitWidth (discrW : IntWidth)
    (branches : List (BitVec 128 × BasicBlockId)) : Bool :=
  branches.all (fun p => truncateBits discrW p.1 == p.1)

/-- Apply `UnreachableEnumBranching` to a single `EnumBlock`, matching
`compiler/rustc_mir_transform/src/unreachable_enum_branching.rs:94-169`. -/
noncomputable def applyUnreachableEnumBranchingBlock
    (enumDefs : List AdtEnumDef) (bodyLocals : List EnumLocalDecl)
    (unreachBb : BasicBlockId) (bb : EnumBlock) : EnumBlock :=
  if bb.cleanup then
    bb
  else
    match bb.terminator with
    | .switchDiscr discrDst enumLocal targets =>
      match Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? bodyLocals enumLocal with
      | some (.adtEnum eIdx) =>
        match Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? enumDefs eIdx with
        | some ed =>
          if !adtEnumDefAdmitted ed || !allSwitchCasesFitWidth ed.discrWidth targets.branches then
            bb
          else
            let allowed₀ := inhabitedDiscrSet ed.discrWidth ed.variants
            let pruned := pruneEnumBranches ed.discrWidth unreachBb allowed₀ targets.branches
            let remaining := pruned.1
            let branches₁ := pruned.2
            let targets' : SwitchTargets :=
              match remaining with
              | [] =>
                { branches := branches₁, otherwise := unreachBb }
              | [lastDiscr] =>
                { branches := branches₁ ++ [(lastDiscr, targets.otherwise)]
                  otherwise := unreachBb }
              | _ =>
                { branches := branches₁, otherwise := targets.otherwise }
            { bb with terminator := .switchDiscr discrDst enumLocal targets' }
        | none => bb
      | _ => bb
    | _ => bb

/-- Check that all branch/jump targets in `bb : EnumBlock` are `< numBlocks`. -/
noncomputable def enumBlockTargetsInBounds (numBlocks : Nat) (bb : EnumBlock) :
    Bool :=
  match bb.terminator with
  | .baseTerm (.goto t) => Nat.blt t numBlocks
  | .baseTerm (.switchInt _ ts) | .switchDiscr _ _ ts =>
    Nat.blt ts.otherwise numBlocks &&
      ts.branches.all (fun p => Nat.blt p.2 numBlocks)
  | .baseTerm .return_ | .baseTerm .unreachable | .baseTerm .unwindResume => true
  | .baseTerm (.assert _ _ _ t u) =>
    Nat.blt t numBlocks &&
      match u with | .cleanup b => Nat.blt b numBlocks | _ => true
  | .baseTerm (.call _ _ _ t u) =>
    (match t with | none => true | some b => Nat.blt b numBlocks) &&
      (match u with | .cleanup b => Nat.blt b numBlocks | _ => true)
  | .baseTerm .unsupported => true

noncomputable def enumBodyTargetsInBounds (body : EnumBody) : Bool :=
  let n := body.basicBlocks.length
  body.basicBlocks.all (enumBlockTargetsInBounds n)

/-- Apply `UnreachableEnumBranching` to `bodyId` of `pSrc`. Appends a fresh
non-cleanup `.unreachable` block `unreachBb := body.basicBlocks.length` so all
existing `0 .. B - 1` `BasicBlockId`s and `enumHasStorageAnnotation` values
remain unchanged. -/
noncomputable def applyUnreachableEnumBranching (pSrc : EnumProgram)
    (bodyId : DefId) : Option EnumProgram :=
  if !pSrc.enumDefs.all adtEnumDefAdmitted then
    none
  else
    match Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? pSrc.bodies bodyId with
    | none => none
    | some body =>
      if body.basicBlocks.isEmpty || !enumBodyTargetsInBounds body then
        none
      else
        let unreachBb := body.basicBlocks.length
        let bbs' :=
          body.basicBlocks.map
            (applyUnreachableEnumBranchingBlock pSrc.enumDefs body.locals unreachBb)
        let trapBb : EnumBlock := {
          statements := []
          terminator := .baseTerm .unreachable
          cleanup := false
        }
        let body' : EnumBody := { body with basicBlocks := bbs' ++ [trapBb] }
        match setElem? pSrc.bodies bodyId body' with
        | some bodies' => some { pSrc with bodies := bodies' }
        | none => none

/-- Decidable validator for `UnreachableEnumBranching`. -/
noncomputable def checkUnreachableEnumBranching (bodyId : DefId)
    (pSrc pTgt : EnumProgram) : Bool :=
  match applyUnreachableEnumBranching pSrc bodyId with
  | some pOut => enumProgramEq pOut pTgt
  | none => false

/-! ### Pass B: Certified `EnumScalarize` Lowering Directly Into Unmodified `Trusted.MirAst` -/

/-- Plan identifying a single internal `AdtEnum` local (`enumLocal > argumentCount`)
in `defId` to scalarize into flat `Trusted.MirSemantics.isSupportedScalarOrUnitTy`
locals. -/
structure EnumScalarizePlan where
  defId : DefId
  enumLocal : LocalId

/-- Finite sequence of `EnumScalarizePlan` steps. -/
abbrev EnumScalarizeTrace := List EnumScalarizePlan

/-- Compute variant payload base offset inside the flattened payload local block
of a `.direct` enum: sum of `vd.fields.length` for preceding variants `0 .. v - 1`. -/
noncomputable def directVariantFieldOffset : List VariantDef → Nat → Nat
  | [], _ => 0
  | _, 0 => 0
  | vd :: rest, v + 1 => vd.fields.length + directVariantFieldOffset rest v

/-- Flatten all `VariantDef.fields` of `ed.variants` in declaration order. -/
noncomputable def flattenAllVariantFieldTys (ed : AdtEnumDef) : List MirTy :=
  listFlatMap (fun vd => vd.fields) ed.variants

/-- Extract the non-niche `extraFields` `MirTy` list (`f ≠ nicheField`) of
`untagged` in a `.niche` enum. -/
noncomputable def nicheExtraFieldTysAux (nicheField : Nat) :
    Nat → List MirTy → List MirTy
  | _, [] => []
  | idx, ty :: rest =>
    if Nat.beq idx nicheField then
      nicheExtraFieldTysAux nicheField (idx + 1) rest
    else
      ty :: nicheExtraFieldTysAux nicheField (idx + 1) rest

/-- Maximum `AggregateEnum` arity of `ed` (`max_{vd} vd.fields.length`), used to
allocate typed scratch locals for left-to-right operand evaluation before
destination `DeadLocal` checking. -/
noncomputable def enumScratchTysForVariants (ed : AdtEnumDef) : List MirTy :=
  flattenAllVariantFieldTys ed

/-- Allocate the trailing `.base ty` locals appended by `EnumScalarize` for an
`AdtEnumDef` `ed`:
- `base + 0`: `livenessLocal : .unit` (tracks `.enumDead` vs live across all
  layouts, including 0-field variants!).
- `base + 1`: `faultScratchU32 : .int .i32 false` (used by `subUnchecked 0 1` to
  raise deterministic `FaultKind.undefined` on uninhabited/empty UB!).
- Layout-specific storage & scratch locals starting at `base + 2`:
  * `.empty`: `[]` (`livenessLocal` + `faultScratchU32` suffice!).
  * `.single`: `vd₀.fields` (`F` payload locals) ++ `vd₀.fields` (`F` aggregate
    operand evaluation scratch locals).
  * `.direct tagW tagS`: `[.enum (directTagEnumTy ed tagW tagS)]` (`tagLocal`)
    ++ `flattenAllVariantFieldTys ed` (per-variant payload locals)
    ++ `flattenAllVariantFieldTys ed` (per-variant aggregate scratch locals).
  * `.niche tagW untagged ... nicheField _`:
    `[.int tagW false, .int tagW false, .int tagW false]`
    (`nicheLocal`, `rangeScratch1`, `rangeScratch2`)
    ++ `extraFieldTys` (payload locals for `f ≠ nicheField` of `untagged`)
    ++ `flattenAllVariantFieldTys ed` (per-variant operand scratch locals across
       all variants, including ZST niche variants and uninhabited variants!). -/
noncomputable def scalarizedEnumComponentTys (ed : AdtEnumDef) :
    Option (List MirTy) :=
  match ed.layout with
  | .empty =>
    some [.unit, .int .i32 false]
  | .single =>
    match Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? ed.variants 0 with
    | none => none
    | some vd₀ =>
      some ([.unit, .int .i32 false] ++ vd₀.fields ++ vd₀.fields)
  | .direct tagW tagS =>
    let allFs := flattenAllVariantFieldTys ed
    some ([.unit, .int .i32 false, .enum (directTagEnumTy ed tagW tagS)] ++
      allFs ++ allFs)
  | .niche tagW untagged _ _ _ _ nicheField _ =>
    match Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? ed.variants untagged with
    | none => none
    | some uVd =>
      let extras := nicheExtraFieldTysAux nicheField 0 uVd.fields
      let allFs := flattenAllVariantFieldTys ed
      some ([.unit, .int .i32 false,
        .int tagW false, .int tagW false, .int tagW false] ++
        extras ++ allFs)

/-- Build `k` consecutive `StorageLive` statements `[base .. base + k - 1]`. -/
noncomputable def mkStorageLiveRange (start : LocalId) : Nat → List EnumStmt
  | 0 => []
  | i + 1 =>
    .baseStmt (.storageLive start) :: mkStorageLiveRange (start + 1) i

/-- Build `k` consecutive `StorageDead` statements `[base .. base + k - 1]`. -/
noncomputable def mkStorageDeadRange (start : LocalId) : Nat → List EnumStmt
  | 0 => []
  | i + 1 =>
    .baseStmt (.storageDead start) :: mkStorageDeadRange (start + 1) i

/-- Helper: 1-statement `FaultKind.undefined` trigger `faultScratch = 0_u32 -_uchk 1_u32`
in unmodified `Trusted.MirSemantics`. -/
noncomputable def mkImmediateUbStmt (faultScratch : LocalId) : EnumStmt :=
  let c0 : Operand := .constant { ty := .int .i32 false, lit := .scalar (BitVec.ofNat 128 0) }
  let c1 : Operand := .constant { ty := .int .i32 false, lit := .scalar (BitVec.ofNat 128 1) }
  .baseStmt (.assign { localId := faultScratch, projection := [] }
    (.binaryOp .subUnchecked c0 c1))

/-- Helper: 1-statement `DeadLocal` liveness check `livenessLocal = copy livenessLocal`
(steps as an exact state identity when `livenessLocal` is `.live (some .unit)`,
and faults `.fault .undefined` when `livenessLocal` is `.dead`!). -/
noncomputable def mkLivenessCheckStmt (livenessLocal : LocalId) : EnumStmt :=
  let p : Place := { localId := livenessLocal, projection := [] }
  .baseStmt (.assign p (.use (.copy p)))

/-- Helper: 2-statement straight-line `WrappingRange128` check on unsigned
`.int tagW false` value in `valOp`:
1. `scratchDiff = sub valOp (const r.start)`
2. `scratchGuard = subUnchecked (const ((r.end_ - r.start) mod 2^tagW)) (move scratchDiff)`
Succeeds iff `val ∈ [r.start ..= r.end_]` at width `tagW`; otherwise faults
`.fault .undefined` with zero basic-block splits! -/
noncomputable def mkWrappingRangeCheckStmts (tagW : IntWidth)
    (scratchDiff scratchGuard : LocalId) (valOp : Operand)
    (r : WrappingRange128) : List EnumStmt :=
  let startC : Operand :=
    .constant { ty := .int tagW false, lit := .scalar (truncateBits tagW r.start) }
  let spanBits := subTruncBits tagW r.end_ r.start
  let spanC : Operand :=
    .constant { ty := .int tagW false, lit := .scalar spanBits }
  let pDiff : Place := { localId := scratchDiff, projection := [] }
  let pGuard : Place := { localId := scratchGuard, projection := [] }
  [ .baseStmt (.assign pDiff (.binaryOp .sub valOp startC)),
    .baseStmt (.assign pGuard (.binaryOp .subUnchecked spanC (.move pDiff))) ]

/-- Evaluate `ops` left-to-right into fresh live scratch locals
`[scratchBase .. scratchBase + k - 1]` (emitting `StorageLive` first so scratch
writes never `DeadLocal`-fault even if the enclosing enum had `StorageLive`
annotations!). -/
noncomputable def mkEvalOpsToScratch : LocalId → List Operand → List EnumStmt
  | _, [] => []
  | scratch, op :: rest =>
    let p : Place := { localId := scratch, projection := [] }
    .baseStmt (.storageLive scratch) ::
      .baseStmt (.assign p (.use op)) ::
      mkEvalOpsToScratch (scratch + 1) rest

/-- Copy evaluated scratch locals into payload locals `[dstBase .. dstBase + k - 1]`. -/
noncomputable def mkMoveScratchToPayload : LocalId → LocalId → Nat → List EnumStmt
  | _, _, 0 => []
  | scratch, dst, i + 1 =>
    let pSrc : Place := { localId := scratch, projection := [] }
    let pDst : Place := { localId := dst, projection := [] }
    .baseStmt (.assign pDst (.use (.move pSrc))) ::
      mkMoveScratchToPayload (scratch + 1) (dst + 1) i

/-- Move evaluated scratch locals into a `.niche` `untagged` variant's
`nicheLocal` (with `WrappingRange` check!) and `extraLocals`. -/
noncomputable def mkMoveScratchToNicheUntagged (tagW : IntWidth)
    (nicheLocal scratchDiff scratchGuard extraBase scratchBase nicheField : Nat)
    (uRange : WrappingRange128) : Nat → List MirTy → List EnumStmt
  | _, [] => []
  | idx, _ :: rest =>
    let pScr : Place := { localId := scratchBase + idx, projection := [] }
    if Nat.beq idx nicheField then
      mkWrappingRangeCheckStmts tagW scratchDiff scratchGuard (.copy pScr) uRange ++
        [.baseStmt (.assign { localId := nicheLocal, projection := [] }
          (.use (.move pScr)))] ++
        mkMoveScratchToNicheUntagged tagW nicheLocal scratchDiff scratchGuard
          extraBase scratchBase nicheField uRange (idx + 1) rest
    else
      let eSlot := extraBase + nicheExtraIdx nicheField idx
      .baseStmt (.assign { localId := eSlot, projection := [] }
        (.use (.move pScr))) ::
        mkMoveScratchToNicheUntagged tagW nicheLocal scratchDiff scratchGuard
          extraBase scratchBase nicheField uRange (idx + 1) rest

/-- Clean non-self-referential static check on `stmt : EnumStmt` for `enumLocal`. -/
noncomputable def checkStmtForEnumLocal (decls : List EnumLocalDecl)
    (enumLocal : LocalId) (ed : AdtEnumDef) : EnumStmt → Bool
  | .baseStmt (.storageLive _) => true
  | .baseStmt (.storageDead id) => !Nat.beq id 0
  | .baseStmt (.assign dst rval) =>
    !Nat.beq dst.localId enumLocal && !rvalueMentionsLocal enumLocal rval
  | .baseStmt .nop => true
  | .baseStmt .unsupported => false
  | .setDiscriminant l v =>
    if !Nat.beq l enumLocal then true else Nat.blt v ed.variants.length
  | .assignField l v f rval =>
    if !Nat.beq l enumLocal then
      !rvalueMentionsLocal enumLocal rval
    else
      !rvalueMentionsLocal enumLocal rval &&
        match Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? ed.variants v with
        | none => false
        | some vd => Nat.blt f vd.fields.length
  | .readField dst src v f _ =>
    if !Nat.beq src enumLocal then
      !Nat.beq dst enumLocal
    else
      !Nat.beq dst enumLocal &&
        match Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? decls dst, Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? ed.variants v with
        | some (.base dstTy), some vd =>
          match Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? vd.fields f with
          | some fTy => MirTy.beq fTy dstTy
          | none => false
        | _, _ => false
  | .aggregateEnum dst v ops =>
    if !Nat.beq dst enumLocal then
      !ops.any (stmtMentionsLocalOperand enumLocal)
    else
      !ops.any (stmtMentionsLocalOperand enumLocal) &&
        match Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? ed.variants v with
        | none => false
        | some vd => Nat.beq ops.length vd.fields.length
  | .discriminantDirect dst src =>
    if !Nat.beq src enumLocal then
      !Nat.beq dst enumLocal
    else
      !Nat.beq dst enumLocal &&
        (match ed.layout with | .niche _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ => false | _ => true) &&
        match Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? decls dst with
        | some (.base dstTy) =>
          MirTy.beq dstTy (.int ed.discrWidth ed.discrSigned)
        | _ => false

/-- Check static well-typedness of `term : EnumTerminator` wrt `enumLocal`. -/
noncomputable def checkTermForEnumLocal (decls : List EnumLocalDecl)
    (enumLocal : LocalId) (ed : AdtEnumDef) : EnumTerminator → Bool
  | .baseTerm (.goto _) | .baseTerm .return_ | .baseTerm .unreachable => true
  | .baseTerm (.switchInt discr _) => !stmtMentionsLocalOperand enumLocal discr
  | .baseTerm _ => false
  | .switchDiscr discrDst eLoc _ =>
    if !Nat.beq eLoc enumLocal then
      !Nat.beq discrDst enumLocal
    else
      !Nat.beq discrDst enumLocal &&
        match Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? decls discrDst with
        | some (.base dstTy) =>
          MirTy.beq dstTy (.int ed.discrWidth ed.discrSigned)
        | _ => false

/-- Lower a single `EnumStmt` wrt `enumLocal` (`base` = start of appended
component locals of count `compCount`) into straight-line `List EnumStmt`
(`0` basic-block splits!). -/
noncomputable def lowerEnumStmt (enumLocal base compCount : Nat)
    (ed : AdtEnumDef) (stmt : EnumStmt) : List EnumStmt :=
  let liveLoc := base
  let faultLoc := base + 1
  match stmt with
  | .baseStmt (.storageLive id) =>
    if Nat.beq id enumLocal then
      .baseStmt (.storageLive enumLocal) :: mkStorageLiveRange base compCount
    else
      [stmt]
  | .baseStmt (.storageDead id) =>
    if Nat.beq id enumLocal then
      .baseStmt (.storageDead enumLocal) :: mkStorageDeadRange base compCount
    else
      [stmt]
  | .baseStmt _ => [stmt]
  | .setDiscriminant l v =>
    if !Nat.beq l enumLocal then
      [stmt]
    else
      match Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? ed.variants v with
      | none => [.baseStmt .unsupported]
      | some vd =>
        if variantIsUninhabited vd then
          [mkLivenessCheckStmt liveLoc, mkImmediateUbStmt faultLoc]
        else
          match ed.layout with
          | .empty => [mkLivenessCheckStmt liveLoc, mkImmediateUbStmt faultLoc]
          | .single => [mkLivenessCheckStmt liveLoc]
          | .direct tagW tagS =>
            let tagLoc := base + 2
            let ety := directTagEnumTy ed tagW tagS
            let tBits := truncateBits tagW (BitVec.ofNat 128 vd.discrVal)
            let cOp : Operand := .constant { ty := .enum ety, lit := .scalar tBits }
            [ mkLivenessCheckStmt liveLoc,
              .baseStmt (.assign { localId := tagLoc, projection := [] } (.use cOp)) ]
          | .niche tagW untagged nStart nLast nStartBits _ _ uRange =>
            let nicheLoc := base + 2
            let scrDiff := base + 3
            let scrGuard := base + 4
            if Nat.beq v untagged then
              mkLivenessCheckStmt liveLoc ::
                mkWrappingRangeCheckStmts tagW scrDiff scrGuard
                  (.copy { localId := nicheLoc, projection := [] }) uRange
            else if Nat.ble nStart v && Nat.ble v nLast then
              let tBits := addTruncBits tagW (BitVec.ofNat 128 (v - nStart)) nStartBits
              let cOp : Operand :=
                .constant { ty := .int tagW false, lit := .scalar tBits }
              [ mkLivenessCheckStmt liveLoc,
                .baseStmt (.assign { localId := nicheLoc, projection := [] } (.use cOp)) ]
            else
              [ mkLivenessCheckStmt liveLoc, .baseStmt .unsupported ]
  | .assignField l v f rval =>
    if !Nat.beq l enumLocal then
      [stmt]
    else
      match ed.layout, Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? ed.variants v with
      | _, none => [.baseStmt .unsupported]
      | .single, some vd =>
        let fSlot := base + 2 + f
        let scr := base + 2 + vd.fields.length + f
        [ .baseStmt (.storageLive scr),
          .baseStmt (.assign { localId := scr, projection := [] } rval),
          mkLivenessCheckStmt liveLoc,
          .baseStmt (.assign { localId := fSlot, projection := [] }
            (.use (.move { localId := scr, projection := [] }))) ]
      | .direct _ _, some _ =>
        let allFs := flattenAllVariantFieldTys ed
        let off := directVariantFieldOffset ed.variants v + f
        let fSlot := base + 3 + off
        let scr := base + 3 + allFs.length + off
        [ .baseStmt (.storageLive scr),
          .baseStmt (.assign { localId := scr, projection := [] } rval),
          mkLivenessCheckStmt liveLoc,
          .baseStmt (.assign { localId := fSlot, projection := [] }
            (.use (.move { localId := scr, projection := [] }))) ]
      | .niche tagW untagged nStart nLast _ _ nicheField uRange, some vd =>
        match Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? vd.fields f with
        | none => [.baseStmt .unsupported]
        | some fTy =>
          let nicheLoc := base + 2
          let scrDiff := base + 3
          let scrGuard := base + 4
          match Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? ed.variants untagged with
          | none => [.baseStmt .unsupported]
          | some uVd =>
            let extraCount := (nicheExtraFieldTysAux nicheField 0 uVd.fields).length
            let extraBase := base + 5
            let scrBase := extraBase + extraCount
            let vScrBase := scrBase + directVariantFieldOffset ed.variants v
            let scr := vScrBase + f
            if Nat.beq v untagged then
              if Nat.beq f nicheField then
                [ .baseStmt (.storageLive scr),
                  .baseStmt (.assign { localId := scr, projection := [] } rval),
                  mkLivenessCheckStmt liveLoc ] ++
                  mkWrappingRangeCheckStmts tagW scrDiff scrGuard
                    (.copy { localId := scr, projection := [] }) uRange ++
                  [ .baseStmt (.assign { localId := nicheLoc, projection := [] }
                      (.use (.move { localId := scr, projection := [] }))) ]
              else
                let eSlot := extraBase + nicheExtraIdx nicheField f
                [ .baseStmt (.storageLive scr),
                  .baseStmt (.assign { localId := scr, projection := [] } rval),
                  mkLivenessCheckStmt liveLoc,
                  .baseStmt (.assign { localId := eSlot, projection := [] }
                    (.use (.move { localId := scr, projection := [] }))) ]
            else if Nat.ble nStart v && Nat.ble v nLast && isZstBaseTy fTy then
              [ .baseStmt (.storageLive scr),
                .baseStmt (.assign { localId := scr, projection := [] } rval),
                mkLivenessCheckStmt liveLoc ]
            else
              [ .baseStmt (.storageLive scr),
                .baseStmt (.assign { localId := scr, projection := [] } rval),
                mkLivenessCheckStmt liveLoc,
                .baseStmt .unsupported ]
      | _, _ => [.baseStmt .unsupported]
  | .readField dst src v f isMove =>
    if !Nat.beq src enumLocal then
      [stmt]
    else
      let mkOp (loc : LocalId) : Operand :=
        if isMove then .move { localId := loc, projection := [] }
        else .copy { localId := loc, projection := [] }
      match ed.layout, Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? ed.variants v with
      | _, none => [.baseStmt .unsupported]
      | .single, some _ =>
        let fSlot := base + 2 + f
        [ mkLivenessCheckStmt liveLoc,
          .baseStmt (.assign { localId := dst, projection := [] }
            (.use (mkOp fSlot))) ]
      | .direct _ _, some _ =>
        let off := directVariantFieldOffset ed.variants v + f
        let fSlot := base + 3 + off
        [ mkLivenessCheckStmt liveLoc,
          .baseStmt (.assign { localId := dst, projection := [] }
            (.use (mkOp fSlot))) ]
      | .niche tagW untagged nStart nLast _ _ nicheField uRange, some vd =>
        match Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? vd.fields f, Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? ed.variants untagged with
        | some fTy, some _ =>
          let nicheLoc := base + 2
          let scrDiff := base + 3
          let scrGuard := base + 4
          let extraBase := base + 5
          if Nat.beq v untagged then
            if Nat.beq f nicheField then
              [ mkLivenessCheckStmt liveLoc ] ++
                mkWrappingRangeCheckStmts tagW scrDiff scrGuard
                  (.copy { localId := nicheLoc, projection := [] }) uRange ++
                [ .baseStmt (.assign { localId := dst, projection := [] }
                    (.use (mkOp nicheLoc))) ]
            else
              let eSlot := extraBase + nicheExtraIdx nicheField f
              [ mkLivenessCheckStmt liveLoc,
                .baseStmt (.assign { localId := dst, projection := [] }
                  (.use (mkOp eSlot))) ]
          else if Nat.ble nStart v && Nat.ble v nLast then
            match fTy with
            | .unit =>
              [ mkLivenessCheckStmt liveLoc,
                .baseStmt (.assign { localId := dst, projection := [] }
                  (.use (.constant { ty := .unit, lit := .zeroSized }))) ]
            | .enum ety =>
              if isZstEnumTy ety then
                [ mkLivenessCheckStmt liveLoc,
                  .baseStmt (.assign { localId := dst, projection := [] }
                    (.use (.constant { ty := .enum ety, lit := .zeroSized }))) ]
              else
                [ mkLivenessCheckStmt liveLoc, .baseStmt .unsupported ]
            | _ => [ mkLivenessCheckStmt liveLoc, .baseStmt .unsupported ]
          else
            [ mkLivenessCheckStmt liveLoc, .baseStmt .unsupported ]
        | _, _ => [.baseStmt .unsupported]
      | _, _ => [.baseStmt .unsupported]
  | .aggregateEnum dst v ops =>
    if !Nat.beq dst enumLocal then
      [stmt]
    else
      match ed.layout, Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? ed.variants v with
      | _, none => [.baseStmt .unsupported]
      | .single, some vd =>
        let pBase := base + 2
        let sBase := base + 2 + vd.fields.length
        mkEvalOpsToScratch sBase ops ++
          [mkLivenessCheckStmt liveLoc] ++
          (if variantIsUninhabited vd then
             [mkImmediateUbStmt faultLoc]
           else
             mkMoveScratchToPayload sBase pBase vd.fields.length)
      | .direct tagW tagS, some vd =>
        let tagLoc := base + 2
        let allFs := flattenAllVariantFieldTys ed
        let vOff := directVariantFieldOffset ed.variants v
        let pBase := base + 3 + vOff
        let sBase := base + 3 + allFs.length + vOff
        let ety := directTagEnumTy ed tagW tagS
        let tBits := truncateBits tagW (BitVec.ofNat 128 vd.discrVal)
        let cOp : Operand := .constant { ty := .enum ety, lit := .scalar tBits }
        mkEvalOpsToScratch sBase ops ++
          [mkLivenessCheckStmt liveLoc] ++
          (if variantIsUninhabited vd then
             [mkImmediateUbStmt faultLoc]
           else
             mkMoveScratchToPayload sBase pBase vd.fields.length ++
               [.baseStmt (.assign { localId := tagLoc, projection := [] } (.use cOp))])
      | .niche tagW untagged nStart nLast nStartBits _ nicheField uRange, some vd =>
        match Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? ed.variants untagged with
        | none => [.baseStmt .unsupported]
        | some uVd =>
          let nicheLoc := base + 2
          let scrDiff := base + 3
          let scrGuard := base + 4
          let extraCount := (nicheExtraFieldTysAux nicheField 0 uVd.fields).length
          let extraBase := base + 5
          let scrBase := extraBase + extraCount
          let vScrBase := scrBase + directVariantFieldOffset ed.variants v
          if variantIsUninhabited vd then
            mkEvalOpsToScratch vScrBase ops ++
              [mkLivenessCheckStmt liveLoc, mkImmediateUbStmt faultLoc]
          else if Nat.beq v untagged then
            mkEvalOpsToScratch vScrBase ops ++
              [mkLivenessCheckStmt liveLoc] ++
              mkMoveScratchToNicheUntagged tagW nicheLoc scrDiff scrGuard
                extraBase vScrBase nicheField uRange 0 uVd.fields
          else if Nat.ble nStart v && Nat.ble v nLast then
            let tBits := addTruncBits tagW (BitVec.ofNat 128 (v - nStart)) nStartBits
            let cOp : Operand :=
              .constant { ty := .int tagW false, lit := .scalar tBits }
            mkEvalOpsToScratch vScrBase ops ++
              [ mkLivenessCheckStmt liveLoc,
                .baseStmt (.assign { localId := nicheLoc, projection := [] } (.use cOp)) ]
          else
            mkEvalOpsToScratch vScrBase ops ++
              [ mkLivenessCheckStmt liveLoc, .baseStmt .unsupported ]
      | _, _ => [.baseStmt .unsupported]
  | .discriminantDirect dst src =>
    if !Nat.beq src enumLocal then
      [stmt]
    else
      match ed.layout with
      | .empty =>
        [mkLivenessCheckStmt liveLoc, mkImmediateUbStmt faultLoc]
      | .single =>
        match Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? ed.variants 0 with
        | none => [.baseStmt .unsupported]
        | some vd₀ =>
          if variantIsUninhabited vd₀ then
            [mkLivenessCheckStmt liveLoc, mkImmediateUbStmt faultLoc]
          else
            let dBits := truncateBits ed.discrWidth (BitVec.ofNat 128 vd₀.discrVal)
            let dConst : Operand :=
              .constant { ty := .int ed.discrWidth ed.discrSigned, lit := .scalar dBits }
            [ mkLivenessCheckStmt liveLoc,
              .baseStmt (.assign { localId := dst, projection := [] } (.use dConst)) ]
      | .direct _ _ =>
        let tagLoc := base + 2
        [ mkLivenessCheckStmt liveLoc,
          .baseStmt (.assign { localId := dst, projection := [] }
            (.discriminant { localId := tagLoc, projection := [] })) ]
      | .niche _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ =>
        [.baseStmt .unsupported]

/-- Build the `k` dispatch arm blocks and `SwitchTargets` for a `.niche`
`switchDiscr discrDst enumLocal targets`, starting at `auxBase`. Each arm `i`
(`0 ≤ i < k`, corresponding to `v = nStart + i`) either faults `.unreachable`
if `v` is uninhabited, or writes `discrDst := const vd.discrVal` and executes
`.switchInt (copy discrDst) targets`. -/
noncomputable def buildNicheDispatchArms (ed : AdtEnumDef)
    (discrDst : LocalId) (targets : SwitchTargets) (nStart auxBase : Nat)
    (cleanup : Bool) :
    Nat → List (BitVec 128 × BasicBlockId) × List EnumBlock
  | 0 => ([], [])
  | i + 1 =>
    let prev := buildNicheDispatchArms ed discrDst targets nStart auxBase cleanup i
    let v := nStart + i
    let armBbId := auxBase + i
    let armBlock : EnumBlock :=
      match Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? ed.variants v with
      | none =>
        { statements := [], terminator := .baseTerm .unreachable, cleanup }
      | some vd =>
        if variantIsUninhabited vd then
          { statements := [], terminator := .baseTerm .unreachable, cleanup }
        else
          let dBits := truncateBits ed.discrWidth (BitVec.ofNat 128 vd.discrVal)
          let dConst : Operand :=
            .constant { ty := .int ed.discrWidth ed.discrSigned, lit := .scalar dBits }
          { statements := [
              .baseStmt (.assign { localId := discrDst, projection := [] } (.use dConst))
            ]
            terminator := .baseTerm (.switchInt
              (.copy { localId := discrDst, projection := [] }) targets)
            cleanup }
    (prev.1 ++ [(BitVec.ofNat 128 i, armBbId)], prev.2 ++ [armBlock])

/-- Lower a single `EnumBlock` (preserving its exact entry `BasicBlockId` and
returning `(loweredEntryBlock, auxBlocksToAppend)`). -/
noncomputable def lowerEnumBlock (enumLocal base compCount : Nat)
    (ed : AdtEnumDef) (nextAuxBb : BasicBlockId) (bb : EnumBlock) :
    EnumBlock × List EnumBlock :=
  let liveLoc := base
  let faultLoc := base + 1
  let stmts₁ :=
    listFlatMap (lowerEnumStmt enumLocal base compCount ed) bb.statements
  match bb.terminator with
  | .baseTerm t =>
    ({ statements := stmts₁, terminator := .baseTerm t, cleanup := bb.cleanup }, [])
  | .switchDiscr discrDst eLoc targets =>
    if !Nat.beq eLoc enumLocal then
      ({ statements := stmts₁, terminator := bb.terminator, cleanup := bb.cleanup }, [])
    else
      match ed.layout with
      | .empty =>
        ({ statements := stmts₁ ++ [mkLivenessCheckStmt liveLoc, mkImmediateUbStmt faultLoc]
           terminator := .baseTerm .unreachable
           cleanup := bb.cleanup }, [])
      | .single =>
        match Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? ed.variants 0 with
        | none =>
          ({ statements := stmts₁, terminator := .baseTerm .unsupported, cleanup := bb.cleanup }, [])
        | some vd₀ =>
          if variantIsUninhabited vd₀ then
            ({ statements := stmts₁ ++ [mkLivenessCheckStmt liveLoc, mkImmediateUbStmt faultLoc]
               terminator := .baseTerm .unreachable
               cleanup := bb.cleanup }, [])
          else
            let dBits := truncateBits ed.discrWidth (BitVec.ofNat 128 vd₀.discrVal)
            let dConst : Operand :=
              .constant { ty := .int ed.discrWidth ed.discrSigned, lit := .scalar dBits }
            ({ statements := stmts₁ ++ [
                 mkLivenessCheckStmt liveLoc,
                 .baseStmt (.assign { localId := discrDst, projection := [] } (.use dConst))
               ]
               terminator := .baseTerm (.switchInt
                 (.copy { localId := discrDst, projection := [] }) targets)
               cleanup := bb.cleanup }, [])
      | .direct _ _ =>
        let tagLoc := base + 2
        ({ statements := stmts₁ ++ [
             mkLivenessCheckStmt liveLoc,
             .baseStmt (.assign { localId := discrDst, projection := [] }
               (.discriminant { localId := tagLoc, projection := [] }))
           ]
           terminator := .baseTerm (.switchInt
             (.copy { localId := discrDst, projection := [] }) targets)
           cleanup := bb.cleanup }, [])
      | .niche tagW untagged nStart nLast nStartBits tagRange _ _ =>
        let nicheLoc := base + 2
        let scrDiff := base + 3
        let scrGuard := base + 4
        let k := nLast - nStart + 1
        let arms := buildNicheDispatchArms ed discrDst targets nStart nextAuxBb bb.cleanup k
        let untaggedBbId := nextAuxBb + k
        let untaggedBlock : EnumBlock :=
          match Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? ed.variants untagged with
          | none =>
            { statements := [], terminator := .baseTerm .unreachable, cleanup := bb.cleanup }
          | some uVd =>
            let dBits := truncateBits ed.discrWidth (BitVec.ofNat 128 uVd.discrVal)
            let dConst : Operand :=
              .constant { ty := .int ed.discrWidth ed.discrSigned, lit := .scalar dBits }
            { statements := [
                .baseStmt (.assign { localId := discrDst, projection := [] } (.use dConst))
              ]
              terminator := .baseTerm (.switchInt
                (.copy { localId := discrDst, projection := [] }) targets)
              cleanup := bb.cleanup }
        let startC : Operand :=
          .constant { ty := .int tagW false, lit := .scalar nStartBits }
        let checkStmts :=
          [mkLivenessCheckStmt liveLoc] ++
            mkWrappingRangeCheckStmts tagW scrDiff scrGuard
              (.copy { localId := nicheLoc, projection := [] }) tagRange ++
            [.baseStmt (.assign { localId := scrDiff, projection := [] }
              (.binaryOp .sub (.copy { localId := nicheLoc, projection := [] }) startC))]
        let entryTerm : EnumTerminator :=
          .baseTerm (.switchInt
            (.move { localId := scrDiff, projection := [] })
            { branches := arms.1, otherwise := untaggedBbId })
        ({ statements := stmts₁ ++ checkStmts
           terminator := entryTerm
           cleanup := bb.cleanup },
         arms.2 ++ [untaggedBlock])

/-- Lower all blocks of `body`, keeping entry blocks `0 .. B - 1` at their exact
original indices and threading `nextAuxBb` across appended dispatch blocks. -/
noncomputable def lowerEnumBlocksLoop (enumLocal base compCount : Nat)
    (ed : AdtEnumDef) :
    BasicBlockId → List EnumBlock → List EnumBlock × List EnumBlock
  | _, [] => ([], [])
  | nextAuxBb, bb :: rest =>
    let cur := lowerEnumBlock enumLocal base compCount ed nextAuxBb bb
    let tail := lowerEnumBlocksLoop enumLocal base compCount ed
      (nextAuxBb + cur.2.length) rest
    (cur.1 :: tail.1, cur.2 ++ tail.2)

/-- Total bounds checks ensuring every `LocalId` referenced in `body` is strictly
`< body.locals.length`, preventing out-of-bounds `LocalId`s in `pSrc` from
aliasing newly appended scalarized locals at `base := body.locals.length` (`B2`). -/
noncomputable def operandLocalsInBounds (numLocals : Nat) : Operand → Bool
  | .copy p | .move p => Nat.blt p.localId numLocals
  | .constant _ => true

noncomputable def rvalueLocalsInBounds (numLocals : Nat) : Rvalue → Bool
  | .use o | .unaryOp _ o => operandLocalsInBounds numLocals o
  | .binaryOp _ l r =>
    operandLocalsInBounds numLocals l && operandLocalsInBounds numLocals r
  | .discriminant p | .ref _ p | .addressOf _ p =>
    Nat.blt p.localId numLocals
  | .aggregateTuple os => os.all (operandLocalsInBounds numLocals)
  | .unsupported => true

noncomputable def enumStmtLocalsInBounds (numLocals : Nat) : EnumStmt → Bool
  | .baseStmt (.assign dst rval) =>
    Nat.blt dst.localId numLocals && rvalueLocalsInBounds numLocals rval
  | .baseStmt (.storageLive id) | .baseStmt (.storageDead id) =>
    Nat.blt id numLocals
  | .baseStmt .nop | .baseStmt .unsupported => true
  | .setDiscriminant l _ => Nat.blt l numLocals
  | .assignField l _ _ rval =>
    Nat.blt l numLocals && rvalueLocalsInBounds numLocals rval
  | .readField dst src _ _ _ | .discriminantDirect dst src =>
    Nat.blt dst numLocals && Nat.blt src numLocals
  | .aggregateEnum dst _ ops =>
    Nat.blt dst numLocals && ops.all (operandLocalsInBounds numLocals)

noncomputable def enumTermLocalsInBounds (numLocals : Nat) :
    EnumTerminator → Bool
  | .baseTerm (.goto _) | .baseTerm .return_ | .baseTerm .unreachable
  | .baseTerm .unwindResume | .baseTerm .unsupported => true
  | .baseTerm (.switchInt discr _) => operandLocalsInBounds numLocals discr
  | .baseTerm (.assert c _ _ _ _) => operandLocalsInBounds numLocals c
  | .baseTerm (.call _ args dst _ _) =>
    Nat.blt dst.localId numLocals && args.all (operandLocalsInBounds numLocals)
  | .switchDiscr dst eLoc _ =>
    Nat.blt dst numLocals && Nat.blt eLoc numLocals

noncomputable def enumBodyLocalsInBounds (body : EnumBody) : Bool :=
  let n := body.locals.length
  body.basicBlocks.all (fun bb =>
    bb.statements.all (enumStmtLocalsInBounds n) &&
      enumTermLocalsInBounds n bb.terminator)

/-- Apply single-local `EnumScalarize` (`plan : EnumScalarizePlan`) on `pSrc`. -/
noncomputable def applyEnumScalarize (plan : EnumScalarizePlan)
    (pSrc : EnumProgram) : Option EnumProgram :=
  if !pSrc.enumDefs.all adtEnumDefAdmitted then
    none
  else
    match Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? pSrc.bodies plan.defId with
    | none => none
    | some body =>
      if body.basicBlocks.isEmpty ||
          !Nat.blt body.argumentCount plan.enumLocal ||
          !Nat.blt plan.enumLocal body.locals.length ||
          !enumStorageAnnotationsInBounds body ||
          !enumBodyLocalsInBounds body ||
          !enumBodyTargetsInBounds body then
        none
      else
        match Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? body.locals plan.enumLocal with
        | some (.adtEnum eIdx) =>
          match Trusted.MirSemantics.getElem? pSrc.enumDefs eIdx with
          | none => none
          | some ed =>
            if !adtEnumDefAdmitted ed then
              none
            else if !body.basicBlocks.all (fun bb =>
                bb.statements.all (checkStmtForEnumLocal body.locals plan.enumLocal ed) &&
                  checkTermForEnumLocal body.locals plan.enumLocal ed bb.terminator) then
              none
            else
              match scalarizedEnumComponentTys ed,
                  setElem? body.locals plan.enumLocal (.base .unit) with
              | some compTys, some localsTombstoned =>
                let base := body.locals.length
                let compDecls := compTys.map EnumLocalDecl.base
                let lowered :=
                  lowerEnumBlocksLoop plan.enumLocal base compTys.length ed
                    body.basicBlocks.length body.basicBlocks
                let bodyTgt : EnumBody := {
                  body with
                  locals := localsTombstoned ++ compDecls
                  basicBlocks := lowered.1 ++ lowered.2
                }
                match setElem? pSrc.bodies plan.defId bodyTgt with
                | some bodiesTgt =>
                  let stillUsesEnumDefs :=
                    bodiesTgt.any (fun b =>
                      b.locals.any (fun d =>
                        match d with | .adtEnum _ => true | .base _ => false))
                  let enumDefsTgt :=
                    if stillUsesEnumDefs then pSrc.enumDefs else []
                  some { pSrc with enumDefs := enumDefsTgt, bodies := bodiesTgt }
                | none => none
              | _, _ => none
        | _ => none

/-- Decidable validator for a single `EnumScalarizePlan` step. -/
noncomputable def checkEnumScalarize (plan : EnumScalarizePlan)
    (pSrc pTgt : EnumProgram) : Bool :=
  match applyEnumScalarize plan pSrc with
  | some pOut => enumProgramEq pOut pTgt
  | none => false

/-- Execute a finite `EnumScalarizeTrace` on `pSrc`. -/
noncomputable def applyEnumScalarizeTrace :
    EnumScalarizeTrace → EnumProgram → Option EnumProgram
  | [], p => some p
  | plan :: rest, p =>
    match applyEnumScalarize plan p with
    | some pMid => applyEnumScalarizeTrace rest pMid
    | none => none

/-- Decidable validator checking `pSrc --[trace]*--> pFlat` AND projecting `pFlat`
to an unmodified `Trusted.MirAst.Program` (`pMir`). -/
noncomputable def checkEnumScalarizeToTrustedMir (trace : EnumScalarizeTrace)
    (pSrc : EnumProgram) (pMir : Program) : Bool :=
  match applyEnumScalarizeTrace trace pSrc with
  | none => false
  | some pFlat =>
    match unembedBaseProgram pFlat with
    | some pOut => programEq pOut pMir
    | none => false

